d first, the smaller orders of the students passed through. We waited 40 minutes for our food and it didn’t taste good aswell. The spicy chicken was way different from other Jollibee\'s I\'ve went to and it had this weird orange powder sprinkled on it which I\'ve never seen before. Worst jollibee I\'ve ever been too.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-28T05:45:44.376310705Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Jing-jing Y\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:121:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVtc2KNBk4wQAn2opz21HuXKCE4Y-aFF21YmWXxRIsBs82ECQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:281:\"If I could rate this place with a negative star, I would. Even with numerous staff members, the service is incredibly slow. What began as a 30-minute wait—already excessive—turned into an hour, which is quite frustrating. If you\'re really hungry, I\'d advise against this place.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-03-10T09:57:56.829081Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Jayson Boac\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU9Ct34Lu_3ZPWsfXZITLbUNwd7KPnBgj8alt0u2297d2d_RLkbSQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:347:\"got bothered by the knocking of the crew who got my payment for my order via the drive-thru. he knocked rapidly and loudly at my car\'s window as if I was asleep inside but I was not.\n\nanother review: August 1, 2025\n- no card payment available\n- no GCash payment available\nI was forced to pay cash.\n\nJollibee Camiling, you keep on disappointing me.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-08-01T10:12:35.784976320Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:16:\"Bayaning Andress\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXA6oBELB0JFnD7AhjmY-QM21PeNxAhN4zbuxMG0sARCyGm5vg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:39:\"I Love it. Great food in a cheap price.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-13T16:28:54.851755064Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Cumi Tran\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWk41JDU5cSR06GjxUt3Gu5L3063emyhcv0k1AfN0ER0zdRZfQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:2;s:4:\"text\";s:1115:\"I ordered D3.  6 piece bucket and family size spaghetti.\nCashier drop the beeper into a container and didn\'t tell me that was for me.  I assumed and took it.   The places was crowded,  but that is usually the case during lunch.\nAfter 35 minutes,  still no notification on my beeper,  but noticed the orders are being filled for other customers.   37 minutes,  I approached the counter and asked the status.   The man whom was busy taking orders kind of ignored me because of being busy,  but after a minute finally took my beeper and asked others the status.   Nothing.. But then he started filling it.   I asked why wasn\'t I notified yet,  but they had lots of tickets.\nMaybe so,  but could have been better,  but 45 minutes wait for chicken and spaghetti only lost my mood to come back anytime soon.   I came come and opened up the chicken,  just had only half breast pieces only.   No legs,  thighs or wings.   Spaghetti is ok.\nSo I guess as long as you take the order,  get the customer\'s money,  you are out of luck.\nCome outside you get mobed by beggars and sellers of vegetables the same as when you come in.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2024-04-26T12:40:41.080181Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:96:\"Popular Philippines-based chain globally known for its famed fried chicken, spaghetti & burgers.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:1;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJWbcYMUq1ljMRjbgM79tWA64\";s:4:\"name\";s:22:\"Jollibee Santa Ignacia\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.615246299999999;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.43721810000001;s:7:\"address\";s:55:\"130 Romulo Hwy, Santa Ignacia, 2303 Tarlac, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:10:\"restaurant\";s:6:\"rat