author\";s:16:\"Christian Pascua\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVElTxC69dVn4hhDclESIO0qdJ0sXSeJzAlgq2Et36Q_PffHGx1dg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:1843:\"We visited Jollibee TPLEX Northbound for our Father\'s Day celebration and unfortunately had a very disappointing experience.\n\nFirst, we spent time placing our order through the self-service kiosk, only to be informed afterward that several of the items we selected were unavailable. This wasted our time and could have been avoided if unavailable items were properly reflected in the ordering system.\n\nSecond, the professionalism of some crew members was unacceptable. While waiting for our order, we overheard employees talking and gossiping about customers, including comments directed toward my sister. The conversation was loud enough for us to hear, making us feel uncomfortable, embarrassed, and disrespected. We immediately reported the incident to the manager, but it took quite some time before any action was taken.\n\nLastly, we observed a serious sanitation concern. The kitchen floor drain appeared to be clogged, causing water to overflow from the kitchen area toward the cashier area. Seeing this in a food establishment raised concerns about cleanliness and hygiene standards.\n\nWhat is most disappointing is that customers should always be treated with respect and professionalism. When a complaint involving employee conduct is raised, management should act promptly and appropriately. Customer welfare and satisfaction should be a top priority. Failing to address unprofessional behavior effectively sends the wrong message and reflects poorly on the establishment\'s standards.\n\nWe chose this branch for a special Father\'s Day family celebration, but the experience was overshadowed by poor customer service, lack of professionalism, and sanitation concerns. We hope management takes these issues seriously, implements corrective action where necessary, and ensures that all customers are treated with the respect they deserve.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-21T16:01:36.273222335Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:22:\"Kim Allyson C. Panitan\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUeA66nPwdCZWRL3LWMeb7PRzm97kZW3w2Ks42WcE2vS726U4DtlQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:1148:\"We stopped here expecting a quick meal, but it turned into a complete disaster!\n\n- The place was overcrowded with not enough seating\n- Waiting time was extremely slow (20+ minutes)\n- Served RAW / undercooked chicken ?\n- Poor customer service and unprofessional staff\n- No proper action or backup plan for such a serious issue\n\nWhen we complained, the manager insisted the chicken was “cooked” even when it clearly wasn’t. Other customers were given replacements, but we were initially ignored. Only after pushing back did they replace it with burger steak and gave a small compensation, which doesn’t justify the risk and inconvenience. This is not just about bad service, this is FOOD SAFETY. Undercooked chicken can seriously harm people, especially kids.\n\nWe understand that it was busy, but serving undercooked chicken is unacceptable. The handling of the complaint was also disappointing, with little accountability shown. This situation could have been handled better with proper customer care and urgency.\n\nPS: Many other customers were also complaining about raw chicken.\nPPS: Staff were not attentive and lacked professionalism.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-29T16:25:27.282275454Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Eizen Barleta\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUwKxq6J9WB1d9jGuLq6SNyjw_6v5hZM3w7nGaBwbPJy9INxxKoSA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:201:\"Expect a flood of customers, as this is one of only two food places in the area. Food may take a while to be served.\n\nWe chose to eat in the separate room since it was peaceful there. It was also cold.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-03-29T12:12:53.682324Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Oli De Guzman\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWtzrUrQ342HMQoywbEI9ODdZI0_pBDg7HoE5G-A44qtKs6-rZwQg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:93:\"Food is good, place is clean. Went here very early in the morning so there\'s just few people.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-07-17T12:31:14.006652013Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Matthew Scholze\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXoDNPLsuqKDA0fmcAS_HHLNlfRLHtyDOLor8TdpHX6Ztxkmp3_-w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:2;s:4:\"text\";s:433:\"Do not stop here. 1st time we left after our friends had already waited 30 minutes and still hadn\'t paid for the order.\nAgain tried, wasn\'t even really busy, still Minimum is 25-30 minute wait for food. Nothing works, can\'t pay at order kiosk, have to take a picture with your phone of order number, it doesn\'t even spit out a ticket.\nLimited seating and cleaning is slow.\n\nGo somewhere else.\nAmongst worst Jollibee I\'ve experienced.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-12-30T09:58:56.958429125Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:96:\"Popular Philippines-based chain globally known for its famed fried chicken, spaghetti & burgers.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:13;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ06uLPnM5kTMRWwMATVHytrs\";s:4:\"name\";s:23:\"Jollibee Carmen Rosales\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.8837098;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.59823879999999;s:7:\"address\";s:72:\"Along, VHJX+W2M, MacArthur Hwy, Carmen, Rosales, Pangasinan, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:10:\"restaurant\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.1;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:672;s:7:\"reviews\";i:672;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:494:\