QPE/photos/AVoNoXRNW-23qimS0QXb_2yyZy8oEnDP6QECGQ8P3sXUrBwSmpBc2a2QWdA6XMabPsDalZ4y_ChSDcCr3Mo76b041BvcAd_1ydOS274Imu7eO7mDrErbqsfLU0nE6IUiUXhp_XdycO3ROs0otvdUWvw1KjsLy53B1VS8wQiBSNkCZlfCUrGLYeP3PvBgAeWU8sYSx80r45mbfmnYP7xRDkGMkymrP9WUvTN3cxe3_q5E7TzzwWRct0njv_jGhvY5Lz_kfW7SElFDkLGCFDUMHlCoY5cfMROlJTKLSlsd0DXOKo39-WuLWbO_bltmTQ1AkCdiVAxYFyNyF0MwYRMeXXPD6mzbtPq1B0n1Mx457HQwsFh9enwY-GDnN1C6qG6uuV9Q8s0UTnLkt_SIB1rMk8-DrmnHl4g9fWO0q49EA61o8Dw8oZXx\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Enrique N.\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW0W7fl0D5G-WdoIz5b6rjpniUN7iaDR8s-ETzOZAE94206TqeK7w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:574:\"It was really packed when we visited, i think it\'s much better during sunset or sunrise.\n\nThe view deck\'s front railing area is narrow so you will have to wait your turn or squeeze there.\n\nYou can take some nice photos there at the view deck or pay 50 pesos each to wear the traditional costume and also take photos on the horse. It\'s best to visit with your partner so it is much more memorable ❤️\n\nThey also sell souvenirs such as tshirts, tote bags, snacks and jams as well. Usually they have a promo for the white t shirt (2 for 180 and one coloured t shirt for 180)\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-18T01:07:41.942474046Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Yosu Racaza\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXbNGMb1Cf2ZDdiIxxe5Vf51XkKguoSbNg1bHp7ZwgPJzPQ-GbmdQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:1022:\"What an amazing experience in Baguio! This is my first time visiting after such a long time of dreaming about seeing the beautiful places here. It truly feels special to finally be here.\nMines View Park is just walking distance from where we stayed, which made it very convenient for us to visit. The entrance fee is only 10 PHP for environmental support, which is very affordable.\nThe place is lively and full of things to enjoy. You can buy many kinds of souvenirs, try horse riding and take pictures, or even rent a traditional Igorot outfit for a unique photo experience. If you love plants, you will also find many beautiful varieties available for sale.\nAt the Observation Deck, you can enjoy a breathtaking view of the mountains and the houses scattered across the hills. The scenery is truly relaxing and beautiful, especially when you take time to just look around and appreciate nature.\nOverall, it was a wonderful experience visiting this place. Baguio really has a charm that makes you want to come back again.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-06T05:30:36.573804891Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Marlon S.\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJEXENlBrR_Tor-Qvh6xcT0ouFPEIOpCF5BWz-RjSPpsCvvjQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:469:\"The view is very nice. It is a really good lookout spot if you want to see the mountains. We also saw a small snake, as you can see in the video.\n\nThere are also many shops where you can buy souvenirs, plants, seeds, snacks, and food.\n\nWe came with a jeepney, but you can also get there by van or taxi.\n\nThere were also three horses where you can take pictures, and a Bernese Mountain Dog.\n\nOverall, it is a very nice spot where you can see the beauty of the mountains.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-08T04:26:27.461183635Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:17:\"Don Paolo Baluyut\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVQx4RA5bMHNEmpUqVsSOnuXKHLD5ITF_c2C6sl8lWpVbdyLQ0C=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:536:\"The place offers a breathtaking panoramic view of mountains and former mining areas surrounding Baguio. The cold breeze and scenic landscape make it a perfect spot for taking photos and appreciating nature. Souvenir shops and local snacks nearby, alongside with picture taking with St. Bernard dog (his name is Red) and horse riding (picture purposes) makes this place even more enjoyable. Would recommend to visit the place on a clear day. Would also like to add that Cassidy (the horse that I\'m riding) is a bit sleepy on our picture.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-08T13:55:23.645637171Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:17:\"Lisa Varun Shukla\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKFyBtxyg9vfsLNLeqVWqmmKqFKmPXyLdYCjZ5xR3BtxPedwA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:282:\"Beautiful view point overlooking the surrounding hills. Path to it is lined with souvenier shops. Traditional attire available for pictures. Horse riding and picutures available too. Nursery of plants in abundance line the way to it. Fresh strawberries available. Pretty at the top.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-02T01:46:26.745812987Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:92:\"Busy spot with an observation deck for scenic views of town & abandoned gold & copper mines.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:1;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJs0hWPgKkkTMRoGuurDgtCrs\";s:4:\"name\";s:15:\"Mines View Park\";s:3:\"lat\";d:16.4196515;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.6269696;s:7:\"address\";s:38:\"CJ9G+VQ9, Baguio, Benguet, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.2;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:248;s:7:\"reviews\";i:248;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:478:\"places/ChIJs0hWPgKkkTMRoGuurDgtCrs/photos/AVoNoXS4I2_Sy6I3YdXXWYGCiqYoinbZ_29FoM8H8LL2_3zdLpEkHy4ifvKd669U0rL7a_EbEBzrs2akZQ3xbI4S8UrDScXN_YxcgX5ol_XmJ2T0UDnIyNOq-N8Dutbm5TDVdNd7BSGNcW-26c36XEaXG15cewF3m_FZL1cFSJcIA7gG92bd3_bUtP5VE6ngnHWEHhafm0yQtbgsjrH9xryDBAi1U-ajQAiYS0akA0fXuqpS3ZvtON_SkMFWHe9iCnUKnbKGIEECHgaubYFBSSjqVbXJG9JpXCC8b3JKd1RlauOZ7bXlIssFXoDWDaaUrE0kVmBdOHX_6f-rcqde6fdMMjirHiMkjsRszmKMnp6PpVY0Leif7_hbtybLrBFwN7IcNCF