CK6HKzwzkEBuTQiLVAOdN8pAqE7uCbEmHIikra4ZrAW8aGOLQ5DZ0x3rtJ6jZO7f6umErG03igLRbUOZdby0pHq2x_7wilFlEswkpuPtDdmnbucuExX5SAcmo2j6Lya2h8HJ_JWrua1FqOtu94a-f6vY_BAqkd_46JSdrnY29ClBko1IzjnEisuavJ0Vcj9vh12UpMtWHRp7cqAYydxHhSbuvG1C1c7Q-WVamfIKMPxJXUAvnZqHAvitTvCEYewnSvAbk9QGbQJM02a7kjxlDu9NntU7nCJEEF-FrLZvyJ5w_AbYykEwpGw_KOzpFkE4FX4op3NAKb_f01PGTfIyFvjuT3Vi7OYOhn_-G80XrprioElcYWBo\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:5:\"Thika\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXidsK2avaF3aYLhFFm7xrK-41ZXiqpP0DR9nhzcngobk7Y338=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:299:\"When you\'re in Tarlac, don\'t miss adding this gem to your must-visit list. The BBQ here is absolutely authentic and fresh—juicy, tender, and bursting with flavor. Pro tip: arrive before the lunch rush to avoid the wait, as peak hours can mean a delay of several minutes before your order is ready.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-03T23:51:51.867048325Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:5:\"Reese\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWuDijHgg5_Z177dDlJpz8AEx14uhGB9fj0kCeJJ8n40eKt8Tw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:734:\"I almost never see this place without a crowd, so we decided to try it. Honestly, it felt like your typical tuhog-tuhog, no particularly special. Many say their bulalo is the best, but by the time we dined (around 7 PM), it was already sold out. The pork sisig was more like onion sisig, with way too much onion overpowering the dish. Service was disappointing. Some staff ignored us and passed by, while others took our additional orders but didn’t follow through. What bothered me most was the BBQ being served drenched in ketchupimagine inihaw na gizzard with ketchup by default, as if everyone shares the same preference. If you don’t like ketchup, you really need to request ahead. Overall, not worth the price or the hassle.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-25T20:22:45.620616306Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Ligaya Reyes\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWFdMg70l_6TndCYjU8JHS8_9AcOKDA4qjwHC5c8qsRMnHvHHJQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:300:\"Their chicken is yummy and soft. Together with bbq. Seem all their dishes is good to eat but haven\'t tried yet since we only a couple of people went there. Maybe next time we will try other food. Must eat when you go to tarlac. Beside i got sick from our trip to baguio that\'s why I didn\'t eat a lot.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2024-10-15T23:10:46.262772Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:25:\"Patrick “Ricky” Unson\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXo4TkAnZ1uhMnF9qYlU84qn39v3TQHNhLbBKL-VXSQqw_vCtjg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:604:\"AMBIENCE\nParking is available. They had many seats but we had to wait around 15-20 minutes to get seated (around 8:30 pm). Servers had their names on the back of their shirts; a great way for customers to call their attention.\n\nFOOD\nPork Barbecue was a huge serving per stick and had no fat. Lechon Manok had a mild flavor on the skin and it was fun to watch being roasted while we were waiting for seats. Pork Sisig was REALLY GOOD and had some liver in the mix. Coke was a good match for all of our meats!\n\nSERVICE\nStaffers were available to assist with the parking and the food arrived fairly quickly.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2019-09-06T03:13:48.621404Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Martin J L\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWPMe0gvRD2CVaoNtYwVWswuWHB20P_QogecNDboXQZR1ayWuWu=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:385:\"Hot off the grill chicken.   pork bbq is cooked when you order it. Sisig is already in take out containers, already cold, reheating is a must.\n\nPork bbq on stick is so so. Not that flavorful. Chicken also lacks flavor. I don\'t know if it\'s right to compare it with Andok\'s, but the latter is way better. Sisig is it\'s saving grace. Once you reheat it it\'s good kapampangan style sisig.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2021-10-21T12:15:54.571397Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:1;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ45L2f1M0kTMRRYwJOjIPuZU\";s:4:\"name\";s:32:\"Victor\'s Barbeque & Lechon Manok\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.717916800000001;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.5767443;s:7:\"address\";s:51:\"PH9G+5M9, Manila N Rd, Moncada, Tarlac, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:10:\"restaurant\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.2;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:107;s:7:\"reviews\";i:107;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:476:\"places/ChIJ45L2f1M0kTMRRYwJOjIPuZU/photos/AVoNoXTcMvNY62c4gRFXYe_Jun3yDqi7Pc6UgGodTEduRkUdF3iiyMdoxlp4qMJCdZ63fe_pWGTicBc6x0V5KruI13LRYsSNZMWapOOZieEJnQJe0l8RjfMisAegzQnbxCMNSsMV8TsCaMxomGzL1wcL_6DkbJxrZf23g2jp-uoQUScGutoltue1mxFcDb-Jj0_lB6qII5Wn-Z3t77T1od8jyMXALmyr2iQG0rwX1IZCcL6I2jGYHfWJ1OdO4gceR27c6gyswZQjRENC3t0UHsRaH4iFlEMqZ6wgG-NQgoWUQSi6V4urkMmXhCY_j92PAO1HORWwoqtp-63aez5Y5_IomT3NQ0iFWwsWIgpHMqc4H-C1wRovsAf8vBB3zUOXwyzMwfFql_b6anl6hrk2txv0aYn6oHALM7oK_9N7BvbhYB6h4w\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:476:\"places/ChIJ45L2f1M0kTMRRYwJOjIPuZU/photos/AVoNoXTcMvNY62c4gRFXYe_Jun3yDqi7Pc6UgGodTEduRkUdF3iiyMdoxlp4qMJCdZ63fe_pWGTicBc6x0V5KruI13LRYsSNZMWapOOZieEJnQJe0l8RjfMisAegzQnbxCMNSsMV8TsCaMxomGzL1wcL_6DkbJxrZf23g2jp-uoQUScGutoltue1mxFcDb-Jj0_lB6qII5Wn-Z3t77T1od8jyMXALmyr2iQG0rwX1IZCcL6I2jGYHfWJ1OdO4gceR27c6gyswZQjRENC3t0UHsRaH4iFlEMqZ6wgG-NQgoWUQSi6V4urkMmXhCY_j92PAO1HORWwoqtp-63aez5Y5_IomT3NQ0iFWwsWIgpHMqc4H-C1wRovsAf8vBB3zUOXwyzMwfFql_b6anl6hrk2txv0aYn6oHALM7oK_9N7BvbhYB6h4w\";i:1;s:478:\"places/ChIJ45L2f1M0kTMRRYwJOjIPuZU/photos/AVoNoXR40ftZhymxFrHoXWu58Fxff7HlJENkyD5qxx4ubUiemn02TT8tib9IVa2uNkGQJgI3VtCE2wdtNNL1DguVbdC99a2UoYX