travel and go to Natividad JUST FOR THIS\n\nAnyway!! There’s plenty of fun and unique food and drinks to choose from. We tried the Bicol Express Pasta and Sisig Pizza as well, weren’t able to take pics since we were in a rush ? and brought it for take out.\n\nThe food were good and since I love exploring new food, I really enjoyed it.\nWould definitely come back again if only it’s not too far ?\n\nThe place is also amazing! The view was incredible. Sobrang mahangin at lalamigin ka talaga. The staff were also accommodating. The place was big so you don’t need to wait for long, maybe unless it’s peak hours/season.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-06T16:02:40.204195163Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Eldiefrances Plaza\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWHYrbrAwaunjMet6K9WpYsoxBzuwvbPZtmUxvv4xlkPMKnoYVN=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:293:\"Tanay viewpoint Garden now are shifting to new name* Natividad* crafting delicious memories. Most of their specialty menu like seafood, inihaw, delicious soup and etc. Standing viewpoint or viewdeck and having seen a beautiful places below the deck with amazing wind mill. Basta mag eenjoy ka.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-27T04:41:05.361541522Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Jeyo Ignacio\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVSUVc-6pIi0NshVwShBcIPGcWrlO8XM6kNauQQgVKCOUUDirQL=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:967:\"Felt the need to update because of our experience earlier. brief context, wife and I eat here usually when we have time for an after-work night ride but today, the whole family went for a Saturday trip to the mountains to freshen up and have our late lunch. Their pizzas are still recommended, but the marinara, kinda bland. Ordered kare-kare with rice and it\'s 3/5. Biggest let off was that the place was swarming with flies. Not just one or two that you can shoo off but dozens! My in-laws were expressing their discomfort saying they can\'t eat peacefully because we constantly had to shoo off the flies! We\'re right in front of the cashier and they can see us struggling but no one bothered to ask us what we need nor apologize. We had to call them out before they gave us a couple of tiny candles and a fly-repellent thing but it didn\'t help much.\nFamily left disappointed even if the food was great. Not the service we expected given the 950 peso service charge.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-13T13:23:01.734795502Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Shayne Castillo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWgKa8UIVcUUALBqlxu170fkTdKp-aqVQRzNqtQz24D_4n5tmcyAg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:178:\"Our visit was great! The food was delicious, and the coffee was a true masterpiece. The staff were super friendly, and the amazing view, complete with wind turbines, was a bonus!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-20T05:50:48.079259754Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"JC Rides\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:119:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUpHdWWuIJWgLNkNVBN16rAlj2l5giu3uIEYbIyqcKEZgrAHrWU=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:339:\"A hot coffee on a cold rainy day with a mountain view. Best ever.\nSome wanted sea of clouds. We are in the clouds. Hahaha.\nTheir sisig pizza was great not to overpowering on the sisig sauce. Coffee is freshly ground and the hot chocolate is the same with the one I drank in Sagada.\nGood first rest point wheng trying the Batman North Loop.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-10-06T08:31:40.090087429Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:15;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJL1lvVVQHlzMR9f8wfwIlXts\";s:4:\"name\";s:52:\"The Viewpoint Grape & Dragon Fruit Farm + Bambu Cafe\"