TAHO LATTE!!! I would really travel and go to Natividad JUST FOR THIS\n\nAnyway!! There’s plenty of fun and unique food and drinks to choose from. We tried the Bicol Express Pasta and Sisig Pizza as well, weren’t able to take pics since we were in a rush ? and brought it for take out.\n\nThe food were good and since I love exploring new food, I really enjoyed it.\nWould definitely come back again if only it’s not too far ?\n\nThe place is also amazing! The view was incredible. Sobrang mahangin at lalamigin ka talaga. The staff were also accommodating. The place was big so you don’t need to wait for long, maybe unless it’s peak hours/season.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-06T16:02:40.204195163Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:22:\"Eldienameta de Francia\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVP3VMnYDJ8j0pZWnhGB8lvaTSILBuAk6QpZv8VxzGS5zyS0Gg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:293:\"Tanay viewpoint Garden now are shifting to new name* Natividad* crafting delicious memories. Most of their specialty menu like seafood, inihaw, delicious soup and etc. Standing viewpoint or viewdeck and having seen a beautiful places below the deck with amazing wind mill. Basta mag eenjoy ka.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-27T04:41:05.361541522Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Jeyo Ignacio\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVSUVc-6pIi0NshVwShBcIPGcWrlO8XM6kNauQQgVKCOUUDirQL=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:967:\"Felt the need to update because of our experience earlier. brief context, wife and I eat here usually when we have time for an after-work night ride but today, the whole family went for a Saturday trip to the mountains to freshen up and have our late lunch. Their pizzas are still recommended, but the marinara, kinda bland. Ordered kare-kare with rice and it\'s 3/5. Biggest let off was that the place was swarming with flies. Not just one or two that you can shoo off but dozens! My in-laws were expressing their discomfort saying they can\'t eat peacefully because we constantly had to shoo off the flies! We\'re right in front of the cashier and they can see us struggling but no one bothered to ask us what we need nor apologize. We had to call them out before they gave us a couple of tiny candles and a fly-repellent thing but it didn\'t help much.\nFamily left disappointed even if the food was great. Not the service we expected given the 950 peso service charge.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-13T13:23:01.734795502Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"JC Rides\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:119:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUpHdWWuIJWgLNkNVBN16rAlj2l5giu3uIEYbIyqcKEZgrAHrWU=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:339:\"A hot coffee on a cold rainy day with a mountain view. Best ever.\nSome wanted sea of clouds. We are in the clouds. Hahaha.\nTheir sisig pizza was great not to overpowering on the sisig sauce. Coffee is freshly ground and the hot chocolate is the same with the one I drank in Sagada.\nGood first rest point wheng trying the Batman North Loop.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-10-06T08:31:40.090087429Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:23:\"Ralph Jernie Panganiban\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUR5Oc2EKesGsXgVsSnodSTRICdJ4p4aM49JlvBwXtBtmEUBa3X6g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:1763:\"A good place to enjoy alfresco dining with some room for improvement\n\nFirstly the flies are abundant here. Need to constantly swing your hands to put them away, especially when eating.\n\nNeed to follow up just for them to hand over the menu.\nThe waiter doesn\'t interact as the menu is just placed on the tabletop.\nWaiters don\'t repeat the orders for you to verify if it\'s correct and complete.\n\nFood taste: average\nIt\'s like getting what you paid for\n\nTalsilog cold (room temp.) yellow rice when served\nAlso the eggs. It\'s like they prepared it beforehand and just assembled it when you ordered.\nTapa is good, above average taste compared to other tapa we tried. But the serving size of the tapa is small for the price.\n\nChicken wings average taste but it\'s crispy.\nWe ordered the garlic parmesan flavor. The flavoring is just sprinkled on top and not mixed like the typical Korean-style chickens from other restaurants.\n\nThe pasta is overcooked and the bread they used is not toasted with a weird aftertaste on the bread.\nSpanish sardines with salted eggs are not recommended in my opinion.\n\nCoffee-based drinks are ok, hence their name Café\nAnd they take pride in their Coffee beans\n\nThe pastries were not to my liking as we ordered their table cheesecake.\nI just don\'t like the tanginess of the cheesecake plus the bitter taste of tablea is not a good combination in my opinion.\n\nOverall\nPlace is spacious\nQuite windy and not hot even at lunchtime\nService can be improved to justify the 10% service charge.\nA small improvement in the food quality. Serve it hot and cook the food correctly.\nFlies should be addressed as it takes away the good dining experience\nThe pricing-to-food ratio is good\n\nA good place to spend your time and have a quick meal with a view\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-05-10T16:19:10.187652Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:15;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJL1lvVVQHlzMR9f8wfwIlXts\";s:4:\"name\";s:52:\"The Viewpoint Grape & Dragon Fruit Farm + Bambu Cafe\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.960402799999999;s:3:\"lng\";d:121.0142624;s:7:\"address\";s:52:\"P.Basa Street, San Rafael, 3008 Bulacan, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:10:\"restaurant\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.4;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:47;s:7:\"reviews\";i:47;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:476:\"places/ChIJL1lvVVQ