;i:4;s:476:\"places/ChIJrxMbPCOjkTMRA15Ed28P54A/photos/AVoNoXS6BedTJ_ebpfTGqE7PJVhvA4oVRCBjXL1SreC2zNA3dRm5odCrE7I3MV0jIvVVi7meNQOax2a_M7I88pM4WtXR1_lFCwAW8mx5mCdjMYAbZiCIPhD2LHG5qLea44ZeKUzQ_447ufE3NecNPo6n5C01uVX0_JwmbGX4N8jb7_9rgNE7NhSZkqz07twkUTg7QL4ztkFuqQVbsgIwG0gKLy9i9U0GFVMp5Ya9p5M1k29KiGBJFrAxv_c1bdREOivn9o2VFDVeusL0Za099TDh2vhi7P2SDtagQxIW595QeNZeSYs3RV44A7ttDPrgNbEKYfqvwc0iZD9aI4-LnwEPO7y_5kyS7DhU9YveMhEZjYbU4OtKz8rW7rXwJLWygJ8iou68xPDTHrD_-FmslaufB9QGT1-Aq7xfTb-mVW9Uh9R1rA\";i:5;s:473:\"places/ChIJrxMbPCOjkTMRA15Ed28P54A/photos/AVoNoXQlqje0XkKASmd0wNtPYla-Hui24r6NYYlqjufgH33FpaSbsSfwbENz3A50bAoc2dfPHAXzkJKVnE29O1wOBJ8m6CbLEmo2ikp6ycNugUQs3f3xI2lcHPk8-fL0F-raMuGb_aVvxBZ3vg_-Xx3C-LmYCVL9_PJIsB9RKtVQW3kgKJPvWRHGUogNbBDvBm8NCiQ062gtav-Yasj2UskW9eKopQ8uKN8q31Lj2PAsYFqtar_6XqU48bc7Bexm_PZtT7JCkIO4nfgibwPcESLj6hgcNFZXVSONn63qk-a83BkYtf_42oEYFxdYr48WGtUaCZh-xfcFXY-5OeCEhZcfjBtAeWlvb6HYkPN7znYvOb0oLLrvmWyxsrUm078i-ugyPI0tcQxWidV1dxWCZZvyWwuZen-QlPK5vLefIA2hdH8\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:25:\"Sheena “Shin” Guibong\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUZ-qVH6b89Cvk0pkjKf9UnIvFNbeL5SWdQVTU36IWnuB3414w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:713:\"From Lamtang, we jogawalked a more or less 10km steep uphill-downhill rough roads and trails to get here. They have entrance fees, available meals and snacks you can enjoy while in n there. They have kubos to dine, rest room (not that clean tho), mini trail connected to their house, swing and hamok to rest on. Too bad, newbie ang nagbabantay so we werent able to order cook food. We just had coffee, clicked some photos and vid, rest then left the place.\n\nView is nice naman.\n\nWould be great if they can do a little improvement, cleaning ng CR and sana kaya na ni ate yung cooked foods on menu nila hahaha\n\nWas it worth the stop? I guess. For the min entrance fee, you get to rest with a view after jogawalkarun\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-09T00:24:35.147034958Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Jerry Licupa\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUrS3Qk0au0pZS5tGX7EOrokJybSHL0B0iI1O8NCV-TL-6i9CwgxQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:827:\"The chance i had to visit this place was just about a week after 2 recent typhoons passed by so the fact that the place wasn\'t in its tip-top shape was quite understandable.  Upon entry, a mandatory P30 per head is payable for \"maintenance\". The only available beverage that time was the P50 brewed coffee, nothing else.. I ordered the P100 worth of mixed streetfoods (kikiam and fishball), and 6 dumplings priced at P120. As a foodie, It would\'ve been nice to see a lot on the menu that would make this place worth coming back to.. unfortunately, they dont offer much. The road on the way to this place is about 6kms from km 4 La trinidad,and public transport is not an option. The overall experience is just \"OK\" since a lot of other cafes have better offerings at a much convenient location that has almost the same scenery.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2023-08-14T11:55:01.496501Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Arlo 2600\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWBGUlmerkgkvTrEkmqtormf_UfKEhh3dHLc13bBdKCAn6s2CTE=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:195:\"Happy to have this place where i could rest and stretch my legs after a looong walk.  Sipping my coffee while my legs are all  raised up and with a nice mountanous view ahead, what more to ask...\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2023-02-15T02:26:17.064172Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Zyna Belle Cayapat\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX5gPvw6yZAsqFBFZwUSPCNHgIae6bOGViCW4EPhqmyI9Lp6gHp=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:699:\"A quiet place to chill, have coffee, catch up with friends or love ones. The location is far from the town center. No jeepney going to the location. You can either take a taxi, a garage or much better if you have a private car. You can also walk if you are fond of walking for hours. The area have a nice view overlooking parts of la trinidad and tublay.\n\nWe ordered latte, mild ramyun with egg and bangsilog for lunch. The food and drinks is okay but needs improvement especially the latte. I can taste more of the milk than the latte (I\'m a coffee lover).\n\nSadly, I forgot to take a photo of the entire place. The staffs are locals of the place and are very accommodating. Thank you for having us.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2022-10-22T12:10:39.578906Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Chantry Ley\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUi2tkBMBW5uKj1Gsuz9iMwnIHWhRAx_HGebpLYaUJaHn4EpvnE=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:147:\"If you’re looking for a place away from the congested urban area, you may consider this area. They also have some cottages for an overnight stay.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2022-09-08T03:54:12.187928Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:2;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJzTHyfACfkTMRrQ9x9jJUKGk\";s:4:\"name\";s:24:\"VIEWPOINT 360 RESTAURANT\";s:3:\"lat\";d:16.3780541;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.5081276;s:7:\"address\";s:70:\"2/F, TAFARMCO BLDG, Aspiras - Palispis Hwy, Tuba, Benguet, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:10:\"restaurant\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.4;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:8;s:7:\"reviews\";i:8;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:494:\"places/ChIJzTHyfACfkTMRrQ9x9jJUKGk/photos/AVoNoXTjk6Nyg3oNFV6MW6MvdDtMhXvdNfhPgSTyVPqWiyG5BOlx3fmWvB1KPofXNc_0v7-Mi3m7Z_o0b5_uE--QumbT8e5JgyoZANiKc6RjIbeD3NqobHVHhbycc6pkbWCgEqJ5h6Qh_oh7iH2TtsB5BtWowF9hdeq7RKEeuuM84wH__MFDTb9QgPHingJ16LUnY113xdprglQGp2Dn2StOt3eR7G5ktHYt1