821:\"The pinned location on the map is not the exact location of this place. If you are coming from the south, you need to drive about 10–15 minutes further.\n\nI stayed here during a weekend ride, and the inn is okay overall.\n\nIt was very windy when I arrived, so I decided to stay at the inn for the rest of the day because my Mio Gravis was being pushed by the wind. The weather is really cold, so don’t forget to bring an extra jacket and thick clothes to keep yourself warm, especially at night.\n\nBring your own toiletries because they are not provided. There is also no heater or shower available.\n\nIt can get a bit noisy when there are many guests since the view deck is on the rooftop above my room. Parking is in front of the inn, which can also add some noise when guests arrive.\n\nThe food is great and affordable.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-24T23:50:18.239992604Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Hya Dinamling\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:116:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJfaizGSw3HHwfhjM8Hlv0qTfkabte6mvrFP6ydfJBBZX-LrA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:679:\"The cool wind and breathtaking views are incredible. I\'ve visited this place a few times, but I\'m still mesmerized by the scenery and the cold weather. And sometimes I feel like the air is flavored with mint ?— it’s so fresh and cold that it makes my nose runny even more ?.\nBring jackets and socks if you\'re lamigin like me ??. The mini falls are also instagramable and worth stopping by.\nWhat I\'m not fond of is the road — it\'s always under construction due to either landslides or poor placement of roads on the terrain.\n\nAlso, go there with caution, especially during the rainy season, because the fog can be difficult to deal with — it’s thick as hell.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-11-22T06:02:38.061577376Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"djs exce\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI2xEuI3qh_6ZJdptNNbM3soOr7eXVwY_1Y1cX8CPhCgG0_bw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:146:\"One of the best sunset na nakita namin. Be there at around 5pm to 6pm if you want to take the same photos. 20 pesos entrance per head sa viewdeck.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-01-20T22:26:21.432120962Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Hansel Pareja\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUOZRc8YilqFFRPbCuK81VvxF6RmG6_9zTKrs_AVB1ULG1PvXep=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:242:\"A perfect day ride!  The road to Malico Viewpoint is steep and foggy but thrilling, with pine trees and cool mountain air all the way up. Reaching the top feels like standing above the clouds, breathtaking views, crisp breeze, and pure peace.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-09-09T16:28:28.522262139Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:7:\"Jalapao\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVzewU59ixmZl9sDsHDvzWgPJ0lmEnYlSgAolFjC1L59pp3eQ4=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:245:\"Beautiful place! The road going to Malico Viewpoint has amazing views. The weather is cold, and when I visited it was foggy, which made the atmosphere even more exciting. I really love the cold weather here, and I’d definitely come back again.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-09-20T14:35:39.370956700Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:5;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJyxYSfgALkTMR0DdS5N9zhMI\";s:4:\"name\";s:36:\"Viewpoint over Ilocos and Pangasinan\";s:3:\"lat\";d:16.257128599999998;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.60570639999999;s:7:\"address\";s:44:\"7J44+V74, Camp 3, Tuba, Benguet, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";N;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:0;s:7:\"reviews\";i:0;s:15:\"photo_reference\";N;s:16:\"phot