:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVzcMa7h7nkJCyD4F8xxHbWu9P3ocRt3duv1w0easZvzcRJLJ71dA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:213:\"Nice spot for pic\'s enjoy your time with your family and friends ? full of food and souvenir shop\'s around...\nP.S Make sure to book a trip with a transportation to go and come back..\nNo tax No grab No jeppyneta\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-27T04:20:13.991220788Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:4:\"Yoyo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVa74JZcfT_a_1T81y0ePxhfwnjeiXmhYG_Dcq1eqwIVApOyT4=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:154:\"A must see when driving up to Baguio, iconic structure with lots of history and a great pit stop for snacks and some air. Amazing view but also very busy!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-17T17:01:46.607218299Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Kely Talic\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWwBdFgtktOFm6IAw06KaiwqAMmlp7it6Ues-OyyLkGSgVDA_s=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:415:\"Just like how it used to look like back in the day but now with a new coat of fresh paint. It’s been years since I last saw this and I was shocked but also impressed that there’s stalls and houses beside it now. It’s a popular tourist spot so there’s a parking lot (for small and big vehicles) before reaching the Lion’s Head and another one infront of the Lion’s Head across the street for motorcycles.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-21T12:02:02.343081238Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:85:\"Landmark statue of a lion\'s head standing 40 ft. tall on the side of a mountain road.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}}',1788848501),('laravel-cache-rapidapi_search_90c649c67e8b48681108548b1579d2e9_15.64_120.411','a:20:{i:0;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJyxxj3zqzljMRRksYD