eHHBmkKFiy-uRXKQIoJ2rHlLwQsePFloFIHy8nTxviEi7U9z6W7g\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"DenLyn TV\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWttZCpOO0ICYjDTItlfqMaKm9cj17ZSwqzwHUn7Ft4hweFQF29=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:94:\"very good place to go if you want to have a peaceful place to relax and drink a cup of coffee.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-25T13:51:33.130796791Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Craig Williams\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:121:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXVycbcmz-RvDOUgkx8Apt-9WO_G_0wAmWHoNCb_3qJRSyZo9iQnA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:743:\"Now this is my observation. The place is absolutely beautiful but when we walked up to the top into the spruce trees. We was met with so much trash that sloult this beautiful landscape. The baranguay should be ashamed of themselves for letting this happen. Sometimes you pay an environment fee but what is that used for? Because it ain\'t used for collecting trash. Filipinos or foreigners need to be disciplined and take their basura with them. You have a beautiful country, beautiful and friendly people but this makes me sad. Put trash cans up there and once a week go collect the trash. It\'s not difficult. Like I said the baranguay officials should be ashamed of themselves. If you want people to visit then do the right thing. Disgusting.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-23T02:19:28.883313740Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Monte Carlo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWAD9mUy8tVXiEwSqPFyFELWiQEN5vcCbYyRWpniOaE8Bx7YZXe=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:350:\"This place is often called Sitio Tala by the visitors, but according to the locals—mostly Aetas—it is actually part of Sitio Agus. Despite the name confusion, the area remains a quiet, relaxing, and refreshingly cold spot to visit. I just hope that visitors will be responsible and avoid littering to keep this beautiful place clean and pristine.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-02-12T15:21:48.630518Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:3:\"J M\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUzakGUI2y9WMO-ltp823POc0xX0vS4FnFF9XfHIY1j8JTeJDf77A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:139:\"Breath-taking, panoramic view of the majestic Zambales Mountain Range. Sadly, road construction destroyed forest areas and mountain slopes.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2021-12-05T15:11:10.579670Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"33 and tired\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJpphPNjvP4SC_slh0aJ_DQlWJGDwfYhNrPlwPHBpuXagLirw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:304:\"Who would have thought that our neighboring province Tarlac can offer views resembling and/or can rival with that of Baguio, Sagada and even of Abra (particularly the Danglas road)???\n\nSitio Tala made me appreciate and love even more the province of Tarlac! Thank God for places like this!!! ???\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2021-08-30T17:55:02.266072Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:4;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJs5ueDY69ljMRmG1iPcT2WT0\";s:4:\"name\";s:9:\"Baag Spot\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.3946615;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.3960203;s:7:\"address\";s:49:\"Barangay, 99VW+VC6, San Jose, Tarlac, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:5:\"hotel\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.7;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:20;s:7:\"reviews\";i:20;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:477:\"places/ChIJs5ueDY69ljMRmG1iPcT2WT0/photos/AVoNoXTfpg8myuzDwh0AO2JejMu0x1gGH6b3r2Ei817hNifxXpXXHlICnuHsUrsh7HR40wxVw2ECXeGpI4Tj6hCSZps4A61a8UEycdDgmI-YKPVTzBtvr1R5n5q3A4RspqrfHFyW3BHeCLWRXw4Y-MHEuIoFODetrIcJXFT1I0a6qaH1RX5e0K-QYu0HDu-IVQR