eXynouh703KuaEYRHLB_wys3UmLORAWLvE3jXY8\";i:5;s:461:\"places/ChIJP4oDW0DGljMRZU9R1-5Ode4/photos/AVoNoXS_J1uKuUeXPghdhg3fAeMoM_P_yxb4-Iato5AyZ9U2Y9n7OILMRngrMqjdILNi02iwrOMyrSWWTFQqklEXBxFVo4UfXIFLXwaAgmb4fZmKWCbH7kw_baeevqupF7UTp9Lg6631gICjDPlgO-efufcY5d-sX5l8zr3BC800I4MtyhQOCYQeIRRIy3hRzbvc5s1LOZ-cYM4lXZJ7eZJMgQ-MN6lzJbeXKbYRMOAaq1z0dB-AuO7cTNK-GaHdLCTHqzwDDqewEhHgjLZHm5TzJiEj9pbSJVgIQ5WV88P4XZLBT3dkPlQ1Uqd0QxvfS1kR25OxpGSCF7qDzqQ8eIfZ9-r45gwXr-VFktqH5Dc7_M9yj4jsmKuoYg1uEWkyYa3vTRMXLosFI68ZVFea0llHadufAx4rjnE\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Emmalyn Ferrer\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:118:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKe0jBOXuSAj96c70OQGyy_3Fqzz5IYFwj0LRvoZiBJPYJdwNRy=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:298:\"I had a pleasant experience at SM Tarlac. The mall was clean, organize and easy to navigate. The staff in the stores I visited were friendly and helpful and I enjoy the relaxing atmosphere while shopping. Overall, it was a  smooth and enjoyable visit and definitely a great place to shop and unwind\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-11-05T05:39:35.142735596Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:16:\"charmaine tumang\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:118:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI6DiF3ljcysBatoeoLWTYZ1SPkC2AawXZZuHORLWhWY3yTuuAA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:1555:\"I was in line at the supermarket to pay my bills, and the queue was very long. I patiently waited my turn, just like everyone else. However, when I finally reached the counter, I was told that the payment service had already reached its cutoff time of 7:30 PM, so they could no longer process my payment.\n\nI completely understand that there is a cutoff time for bill payments. Policies like that are reasonable. However, what I found frustrating was that this was never announced to the people waiting in line. If the staff had informed customers earlier—especially those who were still far from the counter—we could have decided whether to continue waiting or come back another time. Instead, many of us spent a long time standing in line only to be turned away at the very last moment.\n\nWhat made the situation even more disappointing was the attitude of the cashier who informed me. There was no apology or acknowledgment of the inconvenience caused. A simple explanation delivered politely, or even just a brief apology, would have made a big difference in how the situation felt.\n\nI chose not to ask for a manager because I didn’t want to let the experience ruin my day. Still, I hope the store considers improving how they handle situations like this in the future—perhaps by announcing the cutoff time clearly to customers in line or placing visible signs so people are aware before waiting.\n\nRespect and clear communication go a long way in creating a better customer experience.\n\nNo for SM Tarlac! Malaos munta ku Clark okaya SM Fairview.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-14T12:07:28.669555290Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:26:\"Besinga, Joshua Gabriel P.\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWi-E9baiWuUXVX7U4se3yi6K_3Fk-VNXGwENg42uuLX9o99PS0=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:225:\"You\'ll find all sorts of shops here, from local and international fashion to electronics, home items, and unique stores. Plus, there\'s always the SM Store (their big department store) and an SM Supermarket for your groceries.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-07-04T11:03:12.559548261Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Supportph\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:116:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKwZT9ib82BYZHk2gADr-zpWEly6f5N9J4d2VxLJbqo5MbvPQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:284:\"Bad parking management. They closed the normal bypass/return ramp to go up, which forced us to exit the parking area, go all the way down to the ground floor, and then re-enter the main ramp just to reach the upper levels (like Level 3). It was an unnecessary and time-wasting hassle.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-10-31T05:56:12.815879960Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"DM Madriaga\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVgnKFSNFu3NCPVCHEyx8glevckd5gLqnb2bw5_pyBqsr1TRC7UZA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:179:\"SM Tarlac City\'s effort to relocate the existing stores to give new feels off from the old set up is a genius one. However, the mall if packed with AI generated character designs.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-03-15T01:35:43.970436Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}}',1789628612),('laravel-cache-rapidapi_search_bbdb625c8f92f0a32c8c116be6add76e_15.611_120.444','a:1:{i:0;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJRZ9x26-1ljMRlexpsd4n5J8\";s:4:\"name\";s:21:\"Kensington Palace Inn\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.6096788;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.4444527;s:7:\"address\";s:49:\"20 Romulo Hwy, Santa Ignacia, Tarlac, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:5:\"hotel\";s:6:\"rating\";d:2.8;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:8;s:7:\"reviews\";i:8;s:15:\"photo_reference\";N;s:16:\"photo_references\";a:0:{}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Mae Najera\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:118:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKQRVUUTfh3WqexgoNX-gWVVPFjG_VUqCPWLQTqlN7EbKovYg39=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:231:\"Clogged toilet. Dirty CR. Very hot aircon. Too pricey for such poor facilities. 50% additional for child 8y/o above. Infested with cockroaches. No wifi. No signal. Rude personnel. No extra sockets to charge gadgets. Waste of money.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-05T14:50:07.516996284Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:19:\"John Patrick Zaldua\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:116:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.co