H_R91RQzB0h3IZCimRGIolTpiLd6EIS1YMYnqlOvc_y3rA3424bI_I32L2Jtetv2GpBYUwZvhBQsjXaZjfAGs-TGqOxmgG1F_f8MdHenvsJX7dDH9rSHaf2GWwR8lwIlognFGz1vE0u7L\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Vergel Sevilla\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWvz-fdKl5xG6ZHxoAK94Rj8BMCvS1lvbnBytDkHmRCNxx_MhiY=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:356:\"March 14, 2026 around 1:32 pm\nI gassed up Php100 unleaded gas. Their price is at Php71.20 per liter. It\'s almost 5 pesos more expensive than in Urdaneta (I didn\'t compare with Petron Urdaneta, but to other gas stations).\n\nThey got air and water, and restroom.\n\nThere\'s a 7-eleven convenient store nearby. Petron gives a parking space for 7-eleven customers\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-16T00:35:22.267292273Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Bhugzta Mante\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLKod0ZkI2KR7qGDMf5WVPb09dKtAtg8Jzpvnue1SKUlRIrYg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:284:\"Discourteous employees. They refuse to open the restroom even when customers present a Petron Value Card. This happens every single time we visit and gas up. I am not sure if this is a management policy, but I hope Petron looks into the behavior and practices of this specific dealer.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-08-28T23:48:21.072158779Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:16:\"Leen Jay Monreal\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXj6bdBL7XxaeZ7Gp9o-dlXKuVGJaVb8l-fNMaAqO4Ltuwuaqk=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:93:\"Toilets open anytime and clean, big space for gassing up, no convenience store, good location\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2023-02-27T16:08:53.673930Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Miller Payoyo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:116:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/A