ngs inside. They won\'t give you a key to the room.\n\nEven at the low price, this place is nowhere near worth it. You can tell how bad it is when they actually keep a logbook of all the guests who’ve asked for a refund.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-12-26T18:09:23.996979712Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:25:\"Daniel Fernando Carrascal\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWgryedlxfGIFLZhTW7lmrl80n9fwMZIxBnIi6iJ4aURZR5ntcFKA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:1196:\"From the very beginning, my experience at One Junction Hostel Manila was extremely disappointing. When I arrived, there was no one at the reception, and I had to wait around 30 minutes before someone finally showed up. Despite having already booked and paid in advance for a two-person room, I was told that no such room was available. After a frustrating argument with the receptionist, they eventually agreed to give me a bed in a dorm – not what I had booked.\n\nThe building is in terrible condition and looks nothing like the photos shown online. Everything feels neglected and dirty. The bathrooms are probably the worst part: most of them are broken, extremely dirty, smell awful, and none of the sinks in the entire building work – meaning there\'s practically nowhere to brush your teeth or wash up properly. I also saw cockroaches, and the whole place is infested with mosquitoes.\n\nThere are no lockers available to keep your belongings safe, which adds to the feeling of insecurity during your stay.\n\nHonestly, if you’re considering staying here, I strongly recommend you don’t. There are far better options in Manila. This was by far one of the worst hostel experiences I\'ve had.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-06-10T06:45:15.238609534Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Edwin Gomes\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJZNvpF26ICDck3BjiWijxl_GnO7yDrdLfw925hiCo3ymluo7OP=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:343:\"Can\'t say the hostel building is great. It is old, one common corridor has a leak, no common area to socialize, plus second floor doesn\'t have wifi, but it is one of the or the cheapest hostel in the center of Makati with lots of good restaurants and cafes near by. So... as strange as this may sound, I will return and stay for 2 more nights.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2025-06-10T01:36:30.601194Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:17:\"Ivieliza Escobedo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:118:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLiC-EHq1hYxjXWWSUOEnxfecRh6zlbnXnpd-yAhL4sbPTCq_pm=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:311:\"Worst! Don’t consider coming here for a cheaper price. There’s no lock in each rooms and so random people can go in and steal your stuff. It’s dirty. And they don’t change the bedsheets even if it was used by another person. I was assaulted here sexually too but they won’t even help to call a police.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-11-27T02:45:00.635144998Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Digital Nomad\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVzbaCkpN3iZ4fmI3U83-aPB_sdASH-8TfPciNpxXDctOSzJBZlzQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:1838:\"Absolute disgusting nightmare hostel! There is no sign at all outside of the establishment so you will get lost & look for it for a long time. When you walk on the narrow entrance steps full of cigarette butts there is no way to avoid the heavily leaking dirty water from the A/C above. The staff has no clue, no computer & the manager Yani is even worse, she is extremely rude, not even on site & expects foreigners to have G-Cash app, which can only be used with a Philippine SIM card & ID, as they don\'t have a card payment device. All the facilities are gross, not maintained & lacking the basics. There is no cleaning standard here. There is no toilet paper, hand soap or bins provided in the already gross bathrooms, nor toilet seat. There is also no bin in the room. One of the bunk beds literally has an A/C next to it with leaking water on the wall because they don\'t have common sense to even arrange the beds properly. I couldn\'t sleep because the room was too cold & noisy from the A/C. They lost the remote so the setting cannot be changed. The room gets too hot if no A/C as there is no window nor ventilation. Electrical wall connector not properly installed, electrical safety hazard. We couldn\'t lock our dorm room at all nor given any key. The receptionist takes a picture of your ID on their personal phone in which the hostel lacks when it comes to privacy & security. My old yellow stained pillow had no pillow protector & the pillow case had stains & smelled. There were people fighting inside the hostel corridor. The people that stay here are not backpackers at all. Very poor management with very poor facilities. Terrible customer service. There is also construction going on inside the hostel. The outside & inside photos posted online are utterly false & misleading. What a dilapidated dump! Avoid at all cost!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2024-11-07T07:53:27.795653Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:1;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ0fd6XzNjvTMR7xOiRtXBKBM\";s:4:\"name\";s:25:\"The Junction at Carmelray\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.208869799999999;s:3:\"lng\";d:121.08064949999999;s:7:\"address\";s:99:\"Brgy Canlubang, Carmelray Industrial Park 1, Carmelray Boulevard, Calamba, 4027 Laguna, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:3:\"poi\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.4;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:205;s:7:\"reviews\";i:205;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:476:\"places/ChIJ0fd6XzNjvTMR7xOiRtXBKBM/photos/AVoNoXQRZsg5TFexKDe0lJed86C0rj9G1vBKP6rc-XrMdGbjpG2-7pT91AMprVxFQMCBANYc5FP3cgJr4nj2cipNDdSub8NbtMs7dupREJaGC_