https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVQsKXBEfcL9i0zFn2i1YJoi5WZm1e5RoknQJJACRIy4vDPHO1n=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:496:\"This place is for you if you\'re looking for a quick meal for an affordable price. When I visited, there were only few stores open (Pao Tsin, Binalot, Sisig Hooray, Empanada Nation). What i like is the place is clean, well lit and well ventilated, good working AC and tables and chairs are in order and not crowded. We ordered Dumpling Laksa from Pao Tsin, it was good with the right amount of kick. We also ordered pork sisig from Sisig Hooray, it was crunchy and tasty not until I saw hair hayyy\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2022-09-22T03:04:07.547128Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Mang Mags\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUGyfoISPvm5PUbvhL_mqMvgn2Z-Hd2iwNGp440yjOIuXD5Jpg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:1476:\"This is the 2nd floor section of the eastwood walk near the escalator and stairs. A secluded portion mimicking a food court where almost all call center agents go since it is a place where cheap food exists in the area. There is a varied array of foods but to tell you the truth there is nothing extraordinary about it.\n\nUDONS, IDONS PACKAGE MEAL:\nMe, my girlfriend and her sister had a meal here at around past 9:00. I had \"Samurai\" the Japanese food stall that serves the tempura, the \"idons\", \"udons\" and some bulgogi. It had a decent approach so far. They gave some real Japanese tasting soup with  rice, katsudon and some toge side dish. Her sister had the seafood dish. All at a reasonable price of P90-150. Good deal.\n\n8BOWLS UNEDIBLE RICE:\nMy girlfriend had a misfortune on choosing the \"8Bowls\" food stall owned and operated by Premium Foodelicious which had more than half of their menu unavailable at this time. She had a Chicken Teppenyaki meal from their for P69. However, the rice they served was unedible since it was either half cook or it is in its lowest quality. It was hard kind of rice.\n\nBRING YOUR BAON; NO SERVICE WATER:\nBut the best thing in this part of Eastwood, if ever you only prefer to walk around and stroll, is that you can bring your baon. Yehey! We combined our pre-ordered lunch from the office with our orders. At the very least with that, we got full. However, there is no service water here. So a passing rate can be given for this place.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:24:\"2017-03-17T02:42:07.251Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:17:\"Julien Villaverde\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVOBp_Bss81BDSBd530WO8-zDai3Yq3fu4xCPIGkG4SThl2p_H0eQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:260:\"After their renovation, the place is become an oven due of the design failure. By putting a lot of warm incandescent light bulbs. The air conditioning and fans have no effects on the heat caused by the bulbs. Please reconsider and replaced the lamps with LEDs.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2019-06-23T06:14:35.393906Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:4;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJM2m0awBVljMRmt69Be1Lcl4\";s:4:\"name\";s:14:\"Pulilan Marker\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.9087505;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.82076520000001;s:7:\"address\";s:54:\"323 Pulilan Regional Rd, Pulilan, Bulacan, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:1;s:7:\"reviews\";i:1;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:494:\"places/ChIJM2m0awBVljMRmt69Be1Lcl4/photos/AVoNoXRDvp5rYoKoEIsa5hqxMLTvuv0JOs19OGrUaZvOqlPtpoG3c4bovolpkG9lnDaYfnyMxg5JTL1OYDiwCP2fInvDt7a6jba4VSohsyclxHoBWME0wUVOUw0I7DueIGP7tSkiy655XsoQ8otAjiEn08myv32HTLIwm5n8pC2XyngGZtXKV1eDeOMR3zrXz7MpVaUe_9kvd1Wgp7Neh-JpEthSaGcBvK196lZkO4D4nvDcUBsy-UrRg8P0DyCaqA0JoU5vzIPdjtvdnhn0n-8mxNAFMF0lQFoPJUTqrdO8AReQUV_dQL-GXo3Q9x2TCE-y1jjhwKmEjcupiI