olds an undeniable spiritual energy. The moment you step inside the massive, high-ceilinged sanctuary, the outside noise of the bustling city completely fades away. It is an incredibly welcoming place for anyone seeking peace, offering a comforting space to light a candle, pray, or simply sit in quiet meditation.\n\n​?️ Striking Modern-Romanesque Architecture\n​Beyond its deep religious significance, the church\'s architecture is a sight to behold. As you can see from the beautiful facade adorned with festive banners against a clear blue sky, the iconic Modern-Romanesque design is magnificent. The spacious, open-air layout allows a natural breeze to circulate, keeping the massive interior surprisingly cool and comfortable even during warmer days.\n\n​? Tips for Your Visit\n>> ​Opt for a Non-Wednesday Visit: If you prefer a quiet, meditative environment with plenty of seating and minimal crowds, visit on any weekday other than Wednesday.\n>> ​Dress Appropriately: As a sacred place of worship, it\'s best to wear respectful, modest clothing.\n>> ​Commute-Friendly Location: The church is highly accessible via public transportation, located just a short distance from the LRT-1 Baclaran Station and various jeepney routes.\n\n​Whether you are a devout devotee coming to say your novena or a visitor appreciating the rich cultural and historical tapestry of Metro Manila, Baclaran Church is a beautiful, soul-stirring sanctuary that leaves you feeling centered and refreshed.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-22T15:44:36.314024074Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Adolfo Estella\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWK8c8XyljE5rVdxdqhgKA2Hp436rfz_pKIDVeHePxCRsoSeY8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:287:\"Very different now in terms of security and orderliness compared to 10 years ago when I first came to visit. Good job PNP. Come and pray just before the sun sets and see the white marble of the Church light up in bright yellow on a clear sunny day. Mother of Perpetual Help, Pray for us!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-13T09:21:01.607190269Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"クラリス\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXdC5s5M8NIAdIaI10K0RJiy4ckBhm-5qU_tOCGuAZDt5MdF5_ioA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:171:\"Baclaran Church has majestic beautiful structures inside and out as it has always been. 2021 was the last time I was here. Still as sacred and peaceful inside.\n\n08.26.2026\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-08-28T06:57:48.785051846Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:19:\"Mabriene Villanueva\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUbVpuDA5reLceSimjcsfrCvBtAOlWjwzwWKg6RM7NvETfvjQ8AQw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:1247:\"I have been attending the novena at National Shrine of Our Mother of Perpetual Help every Wednesday whenever I am here in the Philippines. My devotion started when I got my first job, but even before that, faith has always been part of our family. Since I was a child, my grandmother and my mother have already been devoted to Our Mother of Perpetual Help.\n\nOver the years, this church has become a very special place for our family. My brother, cousins, and even my son have served here as altar servers, which makes our connection even more meaningful. Whenever I am facing challenges or in need of guidance, this is always the first place I go to. It brings me comfort knowing that it is close to our home and always open to welcome us.\n\nEvery time I receive good news or blessings, I make it a point to come here, light a candle, and offer my thanksgiving. Ang Mahal na Ina has always been our refuge and source of strength through all the ups and downs of our lives. From the past until now, we continue to hold on to our faith and trust in her intercession.\n\nWe are truly grateful for all the guidance, blessings, and help that our family has received. This place will always remain sacred to us a home of prayer, hope, and unwavering faith.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-28T14:48:43.823957067Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:17:\"Melissa Penaranda\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUPcdSjuhICOx07q48iOJzEhUe1Q6cIc_tbjbilnnNav0fz4fdz=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:452:\"Just donate if you want to light candles. Thr church isn\'t packed when it\'s not Wednesday and in between mass schedules. You can offer prayers for intentions at the office on the left side of the church. Plenty of envelopes and tables for writing are available. You just have to put your donation inside the envelope and drop it into the boxes. Walk forward ahead if you want to use the restroom and access another exit point to Baclaran shopping area.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-15T22:23:42.496323065Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:96:\"Modern Romanesque worship site with a 24-bell carillon, a revered icon & a colorful rose window.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:2;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJPxN-XiXKlzMRMpp1toc0Krc\";s:4:\"name\";s:10:\"Rizal Park\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.5826446;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.97868869999999;s:7:\"address\";s:46:\"Ermita, Manila, 1000 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.5;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:30598;s:7:\"reviews\";i:30598;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:494:\"places/ChIJPxN-XiXKlzMRMpp1toc0Krc/photos/AVoNoXTnbEWBidrrDvIWtbwMgsjTvX4n1zJOKOEFnDAyuIfGql5qs4emiZjXMFjiageW-ZwSJ0leA7YGfIlpC5P58E4cWuZhG13Ny4mGJfeVkjdHSjbsISPu7EaWimDm7QLmzgBqgfsAicBM2SXegMMa4SVA7Qg4tcgBKsj02mhbOGkTVkkqy_1MO5TCdpBOlyFL0GCDRwAkY0KpKLjQDnA2FU9xRYBK-k_J0VUlCKmnN9c6M8Zl4Fr6PYWnxC5u4mm3SiqsfGOhhcSj1dVAzDBFhucCBfx-eh5wat3DPpbK0h-58IEXYcjJ2yr4rs_q4zk5M