Hc9Aq3fM6qCRbxJVNjsDFWzEwRrFFMnzGD-qfITslUnNDBXIBxdL1iYwmRhX7UAJ3GGFeIGUL1WKU1eL0JSQmGG0ttJuig-9q5VBHwcLP0Vq_X4Zkpqk8RDn0PSZ5CNV_YSDBaj-FVD-Cimfw4C0XA7dvQqJUw\";i:4;s:476:\"places/ChIJPxN-XiXKlzMRMpp1toc0Krc/photos/AVoNoXTFkO0vY9Y2H60DENZRZbo0-3VbYXK3xN7NzfzoMBMe_BjbgD9PkErwcmGgj5It222feoy5RN98j2EVluCNwAtEtrcX5oHrp2kMYCO6mCo-pJy_H_C6K75YV8zXkiEGgrU9IZriS6WUjtTeXcvbZ4qtPL96WMCuuAPXDb4EEHIxC5o_a87NPf76BsBnyhyghPOLJtJaX4GT4mFpE2-70JGxo3MdUb3brPFZL68HvLALdr2KJPxdTGJ2fYsuFks2V74p8rJMCl5TtaZMKGUrbaUwneNHzL8Ci5HCAweVOBC3L-IOUW4ySmpCrTHjP6LyNdec-e_vpNl32S4MIhnmbKCnX5_HpQx7n7gnZwMT_3QQkrv_X5GyvUZre33K1_hekYfSorEOfNx18OSMvDy3M3RVMVP3Xai77J9pv8YdwdYJ1g\";i:5;s:476:\"places/ChIJPxN-XiXKlzMRMpp1toc0Krc/photos/AVoNoXQKh0QS4He3KwKfYujpDquQsC1ASZ90DLlDEKNvw3PXgbUHShT-wYwJ3vJBjYSdfSXDJHXgymA8tgll53WdeC2VrsqkNN1ruC9zRF-aIiAoOQGB0RQylrtjGkEaWs5eGxuBsdu0PbnUBnqRTGYFVeURVWiJGA9s6H5HbdegwGeXrOBUgm70tqFRLBFgZtLhrqP7HTrE5my701IOclIGxA1uZdQplDkqLPlmEkGFgTtPB40S39PEYIad2SSaX_93ldrLZzZswrcH_99EeLjEIGyvDPn8ZNXYHd-7W1hVMKTEBr1t_mkzEYwZ0vTCsZ8X3-CwxiUZkCWaPx4iOok7ZEeARVZlD4HnfzDuoPyKVW0RV5mXBG-sdUZ2tI__uU0TY9oESvY1ZGdbH8VZGXK46wqP-ALsx90W2VPJPaCyDo7XWQ\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Nibir Setu\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ_V9j9Y6ThecFJ3SMOTuVJQCfnSVjezlMVs03gtbJIJ5iPd1V1=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:634:\"Rizal Park is one of the most beautiful and historic places in Manila. The park is clean, spacious, and well-maintained, making it a perfect spot for a relaxing walk or to learn about Philippine history.\n\nThe iconic Rizal Monument, beautiful gardens, fountains, and open green spaces create a peaceful atmosphere in the middle of the busy city. It’s also conveniently located near the National Museums, making it an excellent stop for both locals and tourists.\n\nI especially enjoyed visiting in the late afternoon when the weather was cooler and the sunset added to the park’s charm. Highly recommended for anyone visiting Manila!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-02T04:41:32.192036841Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Craig Mason\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocImKGCtdO7g71n6uVTQdNcwNUXO996RmnUQRGzp6mab6hc3Ig=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:1207:\"Had some business to take care of in the area that wrapped up quicker than expected. Realizing I was just a few minutes\' walk from Rizal Park, I decided to spend my morning there.\n\n​It was incredibly peaceful and a welcome escape from the surrounding traffic and pedestrian hustle and bustle. I saw joggers keeping fit while others were simply kicking back and relaxing in the shade. There are plenty of nooks and crannies to explore and learn about the history of the Philippines.\n\n​At 9:00 AM, I crossed the road to visit the National Museum of Natural History. Entry is completely free, and it houses twelve excellent, interactive galleries showcasing the country\'s rich, diverse flora, fauna, and geology from the mountains to the sea. It’s also where you\'ll find the impressive skeletal remains of Lolong, once the world’s largest captive crocodile.\n\n​Adjacent is the National Museum of Anthropology, which features fascinating ancient artifacts, traditional textiles, indigenous weaponry, pre-colonial gold, and the famous San Diego shipwreck pieces.\n\n​Weekdays are definitely less crowded than weekends. Highly worth a look if you have some time to spend solo, or with friends and family!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-04T13:50:44.445356014Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Huenan Xi\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUjSauMa-cE0-WI2zW_T3PICQemPx52-A2-JVMGSN9Ky7Lm0W8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:295:\"Fascinating ! On one side, a complete slum, on the other, a luxurious park ! Nice park, wide space, even if it is overcrowded, it is worth the walk. Nice statues and fountain jets, there is even a temple, some ice cream sellers, and large grass areas to relax if you can find a space. Cool place\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-10T16:28:13.730736112Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Debojyoti Ghosh\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV0VVm-iV5qg6AJrXqfWSZ2-MAH7uc8XiO8F8HdSxjS_RaxHuKB=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:450:\"Beautiful park to spend your evenings here, multiple different kinds of crowds here - from joggers to coast guards to teenagers, families, couples, artists and even tourists are usually in the place.\nEvenings are always busy and filled with people spending some leisure time here in the grass or multiple seating areas here.\nThe park fountain also has a good show overall with lights and music that you can enjoy.\nNot much food options inside though.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-16T15:29:41.092388423Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Dr. Ajeet Singh\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUpvZJd9QbCCs3RIPR07wHOV8l34Wrku5kFcV4FnHvSLw5wsljkKA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:871:\"We visited Rizal Park in April 2026 while staying at Manila Lotus Hotel. Lovely, well-maintained green space right in the heart of Manila — perfect for a relaxed morning stroll or an easy half-day visit.Clean, spacious lawns and paved paths, plenty of benches and shaded areas.Iconic Rizal Monument is impressive and easy to access; good for photos and a quick history stop.Friendly vendors and light refreshments nearby; affordable snacks and cold drinks.Public restrooms available but can be basic; bring hand sanitizer.Park felt safe during daylight hours and had a steady mix of locals and tourists.Convenient location: short taxi/ride from Manila Lotus Hotel and nearby Intramuros and bayfront attractions.Overall: peaceful, historically important park ideal for families and solo visitors. Recommend visiting in the morning or late afternoon to avoid midday heat.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-31T06:03:16.428103518Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:96:\"Grand 57-hectare park featuring lawns, gardens, outdoor events & a monument to hero José Rizal.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:3;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJm0WG0n7JlzMRKq5-mY0GJ1k\";s:4:\"name\";s:29:\"De La Salle University Manila\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.564764199999997;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.99316519999999;s:7:\"address\";s:61:\"2401 Taft Ave, Malate, Manila, 1004 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.6;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:765;s:7:\"reviews\";i:765;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:476:\"places/ChIJm0WG0n7JlzMRKq5-mY0GJ1k/photos/AVoNoXSrNeaYwEqpI1iPMIVy5fIY3-vJSXJMslsv8__2jWrwt1hbqVmytKYrYWJGnUss0SOL7bKQ9CO1DbVS7l2JRtxHFVYqs8-XSHKW4aop_BJHbOVVwPHSwsRgfAQWR6g4ga5IYO-hjC-aXL9cVWZhRp3i11O0nVNo0_U6P91rdd7WUsdzGvJqW3-AyzlKAO5WULqJiufnZdW1JOrZInJ8Q6NxbxsgpqwaEqTfXSPShMUQELAnhS32VWfvf5xxZEMyjqLZKMNrPBRWivMMFWN85ywJVrATtWMQ4tImjKnxHZfloSygNCwQT2UlMNYt-R9KfQe6jqmjVJ_QcaRL2nYKFtCiDieWGNxMpA9_7g62H1Cn-4U-D7HOeLDmHs1XFQHg354pqy8PCMuDARAV4NYpykZhFyJcsytkUHJcro7U2wH90Q\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:476:\"places/ChIJm0WG0n7JlzMRKq5-mY0GJ1k/photos/AVoNoXSrNeaYwEqpI1iPMIVy5fIY3-vJSXJMslsv8__2jWrwt1hbqVmytKYrYWJGnUss0SOL7bKQ9CO1DbVS7l2JRtxHFVYqs8-XSHKW4aop_BJHbOVVwPHSwsRgfAQWR6g4ga5IYO-hjC-aXL9cVWZhRp3i11O0nVNo0_U6P91rdd7WUsdzGvJqW3-AyzlKAO5WULqJiufnZdW1JOrZInJ8Q6NxbxsgpqwaEqTfXSPShMUQELAnhS32VWfvf5xxZEMyjqLZKMNrPBRWivMMFWN85ywJVrATtWMQ4tImjKnxHZfloSygNCwQT2UlMNYt-R9KfQe6jqmjVJ_QcaRL2nYKFtCiDieWGNxMpA9_7g62H1Cn-4U-D7HOeLDmHs1XFQHg354pqy8PCMuDARAV4NYpykZhFyJcsytkUHJcro7U2wH90Q\";i:1;s:478:\"places/ChIJm0WG0n7JlzMRKq5-mY0GJ1k/photos/AVoNoXRyGtQ1Wl2SP1ZxDEt74NUgCueB3CvJ5fiBMTLmbz2iy8dnCf32-QoJOsoDSrQgDct9LfcdQhg