h1Z6VJuMrw0DGFlM8SpmXitUriuZiVWrNTOOK8cR_obkcqWiWLTA-58Pdr_NJwrSq4PUkKEzABJERhRwalNtnw7dXkAOcIAeLSMEson-uztugqP4VK7EoCFSrfz1i3x-HAeOgeO4QiqbFf_yJscfR9pn97c3s7lQWaXpW1F8M7BSk83iadpAdM4bi0Fm0tRQg2hDLEjIkgpTd6lBXuwavxnPL0gasQS1DeMQnFAL9OMAj8dha_OjUC4nlJlf2ss-eLhLVHsz-B762Fej9bC5UtCVZZw0bV6m4LBhqSYaR0NniUabS0yiIpo-YVN7Oo0oAuS_k\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:21:\"Mayang P. Ayuningtyas\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:119:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUmMxBOCfGahbjvWunuhk6FV3REwq_802MNWAfZa7tAHlcd6xlS=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:268:\"I visited the campus during a business trip. The university is expansive, featuring magnificent old European-style buildings and beautiful gardens. The modern library building, with its multiple floors, is equally impressive. It was a wonderful experience to be there.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-28T06:07:52.260608188Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"Manny Yu\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXg-da5a8zn8eyarfcNq2GYSnijPq0sUNl8cm346u4c6jhtgcg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:609:\"01/15/26. Animo La Salle?\n\n\"Animo La Salle\" is the battle cry for De La Salle University (DLSU) meaning \"La Sallian Spirit to Fight,\" or \"Have Courage,\" invoking passion, resilience, and commitment to excellence in academics, sports, and life, rooted in the Brothers\' call for \"Faith and Zeal\".\n\nIt is a rallying phrase used to motivate students and teams to give their best and embody the Lasallian values of hope, service, and making a difference.\n\nDe La Salle University is my alma mater. I am very proud and at same time thankful to have studied in the number one private university in the Philippines.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-01-22T22:09:15.722559742Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Pomperumini\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWaecmit9KlNlosoNm9Es89bcy2iJYibM2xwCUiJcTSFGCM1A_I=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:287:\"Although I haven\'t went around much because I was assigned at LS for DCAT 2026, and watching Yuch from the 3rd floor inner balcony made me mesmerized at the sheer scale of the building and I felt like I was gazing at the Supreme Court even if the real one doesn\'t look as flashy as Yuch.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-11T16:50:26.128821866Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:22:\"Vivian Carandang-Smith\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU3gBfae_pnQv50MV4UWnt3x9J6GRIKWRU-fYFl77t54gNOotz2LQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:454:\"There\'s a little of food places amd choices inside the campus. G9od thing that no one will go hungry while studying here - haha. Everyone is nice that they don\'t mind if visitors are checking out the place. For a moment, we forgot that we\'re here to study and not feast.  I wish they can install a map locator since its hard for froshies, newbies, and visitors to find the buildings food places, stores,restrooms, etc. Thanks DLSU for being so welcoming!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-08-16T04:36:38.920059960Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Katherina Carla\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXo2UcAo9PyMp2gtUYNf79y3Ou7DqclBZ-TvUpBBxot29n67oli=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:373:\"Really cool places\nClean bathrooms\nLots of libraries, chairs and tables.\nThey also have their own cafeterias and a church.\nNearby there are a lot of restaurants to eat.\nThey also have condominiums nearby.\nEverything was well maintained and spotless.\nAnd also they have a LOT OF CATS... but don\'t touch them ? La salle is really nice to cats.\nThanks for the scholarship !\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-07-01T03:23:49.637517998Z\";s:6:\"source\