wEo9eMPxbjhqqBlyCBpp4JESaJeVYdxKXra2NU4cD0yBuQTbGW5UvDAsyR5F_d1waOqEq9n6ccQ\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:16:\"Walking Wanderer\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXwew7HNea-7jUlLyqgOnDIRZJxQ_T9BYeDNCjH-GyDQS5n7Jw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:628:\"A wonderful museum - amazing that it is free, with so much to see inside. When you enter, you are immediately greeted by the Spoliarium, a fantastic piece of art.\n\nIt’s fun to wander through the different halls and rooms and view different collections of art. The first time we came we only visited the first floor before we ran out of time, so we visited a day later and checked out the other floors: well worth it and a must see to stop by the old senate hall on the third and fourth floor and see the amazing art depicting the history of Manila.\n\nPlan to spend 1-2 hours here if you want to see everything at a modest pace.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-26T10:55:55.960292953Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Sobi Thomas\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVaNr7XFddvPvifGX8R1xAQKjL7GQO_BjJObUxSjW8veoQkCzIs=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:668:\"Visited  and had an excellent experience. The museum is exceptionally well arranged, with great care taken to present the exhibits in an organized and engaging manner. The effort put into preserving and showcasing the artworks, history, and cultural heritage of the Philippines is truly commendable.\n\nIt is one of the best places to learn about the rich history, culture, and artistic traditions of the Philippines. The galleries are informative, beautifully maintained, and easy to explore, making the visit both educational and enjoyable.\n\nA highly recommended destination for anyone interested in understanding the history, culture, and identity of the Philippines.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-02T18:23:08.346116066Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Jenny Jacob\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUKKamFB4WEFswFb-ibSjKQ44g_GTwSu3srvoskiI3sTFwUeHQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:1277:\"I was truly amazed by my experience at the National Museum of Fine Arts. Seeing the masterpieces in person gave me a deeper appreciation for the immense talent and creativity of Filipino artists throughout history—from literature-inspired works to breathtaking paintings and intricate sculptures.\n\nThe highlight of my visit was undoubtedly the iconic Spoliarium by Juan Luna. Standing before it was both humbling and awe-inspiring. The scale, detail, and emotion captured in the painting are difficult to describe until you see it for yourself. It made me reflect on the extraordinary level of artistry and craftsmanship achieved by generations before us.\n\nAfter seeing Spoliarium, many modern works seemed to pale in comparison. The museum is a powerful reminder of the richness of Filipino heritage and the timeless brilliance of our artists. It is a place that not only showcases art but also inspires admiration, reflection, and pride in our cultural history.\n\nRating: 5/5. Highly recommended for anyone who appreciates art, history, and Filipino culture.\n\nP.S. You should definitely check out Papa Kape on the 4th floor. I ordered Frozen Bayabas, and it was absolutely the best—refreshing, flavorful, and a perfect treat after exploring the museum. Highly recommended!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-13T23:50:51.401005698Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:1:\"H\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKE61LPHA5kUMZ574KyOAHRoNIJo5bd4u6HLfZzXYE-E9UdLA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:335:\"Went on a weekend, there’s a queue but that’s totally fine. Happy to see fellow Filipinos enjoying our National Museum. Great art works from our National artists. You can stay here for one whole day and just appreciate everything there. There’s no entrance fee, just bring your ID. Hope you’ll visit and enjoy the place. ☺️\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-08-26T11:09:58.813810153Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Paul Hinlo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXRJfKff8oDN53Z6omTfciDnylcCSzbbnV3Jtk8RSR6aBWfgV8w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:952:\"Some places deserve more than just a quick visit—they deserve your time and attention.\nToday, I wandered through the National Museum of Fine Arts, where every gallery tells a story of the Philippines through breathtaking paintings, sculptures, and timeless masterpieces. Standing before Juan Luna\'s Spoliarium was a humbling experience. No photo can truly capture its grandeur or the emotions it evokes.\nBeyond the art, I found a quiet space to reflect, slow down, and reconnect with our history and culture. It\'s a reminder that travel isn\'t always about going far; sometimes, the most meaningful journeys are found in places that help us appreciate where we come from.\nIf you\'re looking for inspiration, a touch of history, or simply a peaceful escape in the heart of Manila, this is one place you shouldn\'t miss.\n??? #NationalMuseumPH #NationalMuseumOfFineArts #DiscoverPhilippines #MuseumDay #TravelJournal #ArtLovers #PhilippineHeritage\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-08T00:14:40.422392959Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:98:\"Massive museum with collections of Filipino fine art, archaeology, botany, natural history & more.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:5;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJvZ4MeBbKlzMRQ7CLeMYOQ80\";s:4:\"name\";s:13:\"Fort Santiago\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.594235299999998;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.97041189999999;s:7:\"address\";s:50:\"Intramuros, Manila, 1002 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\"