tremely popular in the Philippines because of the dubbed clips featuring her famous \"719 points, highest scorer\" scene.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-10T14:35:22.740989076Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Hans Koka\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXK0jdKGRv0IYHrMQAYsy6ATK-XZtvAJBfYS4mUyBWysw71AhDh=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:507:\"Despite the LGBTQ+ flags, everything else was good.\n\nI do not support normalizing these topics to children, especially in public government spaces. I believe sexuality — regardless of orientation — is a private matter and should not be promoted to kids.\n\nI judge people based on their behavior, character, and how they treat others — not by race, religion, nationality, or sexuality. I simply believe personal sexual matters do not need to be publicly displayed or emphasized in official institutions.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-14T10:07:16.433217760Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"joe mazi\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIcoM1iOyyAlAz7vsGnRZk4Y9LwNyxWn6GfyHXghTpYGWkrJw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:196:\"Metro Manila has so much to offer when it comes to culture and amazing food cuisines. My heart goes to the local community. People are so welcoming and friendly. Philippines is the place to visit.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-05T13:37:04.496008679Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Tyrone Jann Flores\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWill_2b2qIe_hSCou4yBs-FkGWhIBFcE5-WqhE9Y9jkh-t6Qo=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:2333:\"I recently went to Manila City Hall to process my father’s death certificate, and overall, it was a challenging experience.\n\nOne of the first things I noticed was the lack of a clear checklist and visual guide on the process or how to properly fill out the forms. Because of this, a lot of people (including us) ended up going back and forth in lines just to complete requirements. It would really help if they provided a simple step-by-step guide, especially for situations like this where people are already dealing with something heavy.\n\nAnother observation was that the review of documents seemed to be done one at a time, with different comments coming from different people, which slowed things down even more. There also wasn’t a well-organized queuing system, and staff tended to be selective in answering queries or concerns, which added to the confusion.\n\nOne thing they can also improve is the signage—rooms are not clearly marked, making it harder to navigate, especially for first-time visitors.\n\nOn the positive side, the payment process was fast, and the staff in that area were very approachable, friendly, and smiling. Not sure if it’s because it’s the payment section, but it definitely made that part of the experience smoother.\n\nHowever, there was also an issue with the release time of documents. We were told to claim the certified copies at 3:30 PM, but we only received them close to 5 PM because the signatory was not available. I understand that the volume of people is high and the work can be exhausting, but I hope they can better manage and commit to the timelines they provide, especially since some people travel from far areas or even provinces.\n\nOne convenient thing though is that there are plenty of photocopying services in the City Hall, so there’s no need to go outside if you need additional copies of documents.\n\nLastly, it was quite noticeable that there seems to be a ‘palakasan’ system. Some individuals who had connections inside were accommodated or processed faster, while others patiently waited in line. I really hope this kind of system improves over time.\n\nOverall, this is based on my personal experience. I understand the challenges on their end, but I also hope for improvements that can make the process more organized, transparent, and considerate for everyone.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-06T18:57:52.467141956Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"美丽아름다움\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocITF-bdlRLUYrL5uaoIk94NCcwo_r4YeOHNNNOgWhE4ZMpBol_b=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:124:\"\"Finally got to see Manila City Hall up close...  It\'s rewarding to explore these iconic piece of history and architecture.\"\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-19T06:15:04.677418953Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:86:\"This long, large government building housing the Mayor\'s office was completed in 1941.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:10;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ-4K-ejDKlzMRKy2w6k9Km8Y\";s:4:\"name\";s:18:\"Quirino Grandstand\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.5800811;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.9738453;s:7:\"address\";s:68:\"1000 Independence Rd, Ermita, Manila, 1000 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.5;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:919;s:7:\"reviews\";i:919;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:473:\"places/ChIJ-4K-ejDKlzMRKy2w6k9Km8Y/photos/AVoNoXRLrCkYOuBY2K0pZOXxhGx-s3prFWoEIZa8QooGiWSo9Y50d0TKKtJ7AVeuU9p_0wN0fF-A1yfkDNwuvJkd_sj9atiFqe7gEmObWHVbc_7cBjJhyxCAVFSKzgihDWyQs5yOfdmLaWTl8XXATpXJ22eq97mn-NLdkzElIw8rOxPMOHFJ4alCin103ZxIlt_vFMvoRLAcw22JPRzJHiw3JOpxMyzAxq9j7jFd_1wXW2igKhzSuAnK_VhMNOqQssW2GV4NYG3UC6FbT5Qo6qENFnvE5KOKxmVmir-4XwCnMKF-6jykCA_BBtIMmpjF1zKw-RijnYdNfXIY2M-zNDtF5Xk4OZTUGrXR7S8ZwuUMWHvjqH56bpkOah6vwR0nkIDr8VvyEUZ2ns9s_5UtIRoIOARD01M6VX4gQUAf3yMHiSc\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:473:\"places/ChIJ-4K-ejDKlzMRKy2w6k9Km8Y/photos/AVoNoXRLrCkYOuBY2K0pZOXxhGx-s3prFWoEIZa8QooGiWSo9Y50d0TKKtJ7AVeuU9p_0wN0fF-A1yfkDNwuvJkd_sj9atiFqe7gEmObWHVbc_7cBjJhyxCAVFSKzgihDWyQs5yOfdmLaWTl8XXATpXJ22eq97mn-NLdkzElIw8rOxPMOHFJ4alCin103Z