s Manila and it was easily one of the best reception venues I’ve experienced. From the moment you enter, you can really feel the premium quality of the place through its elegant interiors, spacious ballroom, and well-maintained facilities.\n\nWhat stood out the most was the overall service and food. The staff were professional and attentive, while the food was well-prepared and worthy of a special occasion. The banquet hall itself felt luxurious yet comfortable, making it a great venue for weddings and other milestone celebrations.\n\nOverall, a top-tier reception venue that delivers a premium experience from start to finish.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-30T15:26:48.350581935Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:24:\"CHOI the Google Reviewer\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVI1MerWTsuS39DeDzJdarrBzR49jf_xPBmpjOIWMbTWo_oqhY=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:319:\"Gambling is nice but don\'t bankrupt yourself. We just visited here just for a stroll its a nice place and also said by my friend a good gambling place. better than the other two well known in aseana as they said. But yeah if you\'re a kid don\'t gamble. It\'s also very luxurious inside and a lot of rich people come here.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-05T15:24:34.904603009Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Meghann Cortez\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVnGCAcYwVpAH7hfAlGzB18kNEPH_Kj_nNilAPKpKstSC-9m7rT=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:1896:\"Hayayayay!\n\nThe staff and the set up outside the entry of the hotel where your stuff goes through the scanning machine is… i dont even have a single word to describe it. Staff are NOT very attentive they let all your stuff pile on the ground. I was carrying a baby and my husband was sorting out our stuff on the other end and the 3 staff member next to me were NO help at all. I guess they weren’t paid for that.\nThanks dor that first impression, will definitely going to last.\n\nNO VENT in the bathroom! I wonder how many layers of paint they have in there to cover up all the moulds.\n\nDoes not feel luxurious at all even the finishes in the rooms.\n\nAnd this is only our first night and I’m already regretting booking in here. We’ve got 2 more nights to go.\n\nI shouldn’t have set any expectations.\n\nEdit.\n\nThat said, management did reach out after my feedback and seemed genuinely willing to address the concerns and improve the situation, which I appreciated. Allysa mentioned that they are now looking into the scanning/arrival setup and already have plans to address it.\n\nI honestly didn’t even expect they would be able to find me considering my Google account still has my old surname on it, and I also failed to specify which hotel within COD I was referring to, which in this case was Nobu.\n\nThe staff during the following days, especially on the day we checked out, did seem much more attentive and helpful, and they honestly made the rest of our stay so much better. I also really appreciated the staff at reception for being so patient and understanding throughout.\n\nI also hope they improve the ventilation, especially around the casino area near the restaurants. The smell and air circulation there can be quite overwhelming, particularly when you’re with a child.\n\nOverall though, despite the rough start, it ended up being a pleasant experience staying at Nobu Hotel.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-10T07:00:47.631294900Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Kurt Pedersen\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLCLY6JiSnK5qcI69x_KYZkt0llgWAm7IJ_Q4o48hpRLtuEqQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:230:\"Absolutely fabulous. Staff are knowledgeable, friendly, and truly helpful. The rooms are impressive and immaculate.. Without leaving the air conditioned comfort of indoors you can access casinos and great restaurants and shopping.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-15T19:46:12.222460704Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Maki Ogang\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:117:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocK_SsJ2Sc2sQJJNiNdhysI0FwZLXXSceg6ZyZ3OxTLgvPfQKas=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:1;s:4:\"text\";s:1072:\"The idea of casino hotel must give the staff especially the security that the guests are mixed, children will be there because of Dreamplay and Hotels, and they might be crossing restricted places. NOT ENOUGH SIGNS going to the hotel too. Since we didn’t see the hotel shuttle after the parking elevator, we entered in the common entrance. After the xray security check, my daughter ran at the entrance of the casino and of course the security stopped her. The security told me in my face ‘MAM PAKIBANTAYAN ANG ANAK NIYO.’ In a rather condescending tone (please look after your kid) instead of politely asking where we are headed. Are you just operating at the POV of casino? You have Dreamplay, you have chains of hotels inside. And the bare minimum you could train your staff for ar situations where children may mistakenly cross the casinos thinking they are arcade. So rude of your security team to assume I am not looking after my kid who passed the xray first and ran (not too far from us) while she waiting for us to get our bags which had a waiting time btw.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-11T22:14:25.564638898Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:83:\"High end shopping, hotels, restaurants & a casino in a modern entertainment center.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:13;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJk5OKFRDKlzMRwQwO9gF-vL0\";s:4:\"name\";s:71:\"Minor Basilica and National Shrine of St Lorenzo Ruiz ( Binondo Church)\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.600161499999997;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.97458890000001;s:7:\"address\";s:72:\"1006 Plaza Lorenzo Ruiz, Binondo, Manila, 10