6:\"author\";s:8:\"Manny Yu\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXg-da5a8zn8eyarfcNq2GYSnijPq0sUNl8cm346u4c6jhtgcg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:787:\"New Manila Zoo\n\nReopened with a fresh, modernized layout, the upgraded features significantly improved, cleaner infrastructure designed around animal welfare and an \"open zoo\" concept.\n\nThe tight, traditional iron cages of the past have been largely replaced with spacious, elevated viewing areas, transparent reinforced glass enclosures and a massive netted canopy for the giant aviary where birds fly freely.\n\nVisitors can now explore designated zones like the Reptile House, the Butterfly Garden, and expanded habitats showcasing white Bengal tigers, African lions & capybaras.\n\n​However there are several empty spaces left behind by the absence of an elephant, hippo and giraffe. Nevertheless an enjoyable two hour nature and animal themed escape in the middle of our urban jungle.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-10T10:29:18.567681971Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Ron Matthew Turing\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:119:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU6UMn5tmLjCaNGolLICX885jHtmnXoV1481K9tRWeaSr5k2Xhw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:392:\"The park is highly organized, paved, and fully wheelchair accessible. The air smells much cleaner now due to a new sewage treatment system. However, long-time visitors will notice that the zoo feels a bit empty. Famous residents like Mali the elephant and Bertha the hippo have passed away. You will still see tigers, lions, and monkeys, but do not expect a massive variety of large wildlife.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-09T09:51:00.276268206Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:4:\"Abby\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXzo2ibvZwc0z1TdWPDHOqJxoPuFtOnRbrc94fOkRKYUBqY40Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:317:\"A nice an lovely place to hangout but don\'t expect much animals. There are lots of birds few of other animals. The Capybaras and turtles are the ones carrying the show here. You can buy tickets in advance online by searching manila zoo website. Overall great experience if you just wanna watch animals do their thing.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-01-23T11:48:02.185187212Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Pavenjitkaur Bring\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWzraJpdR8HTaxZ0ZoFZTPeza8GPLKJkzioAyNdh4hv_HmZ6qam=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:493:\"It was the best experience ever as a first timer, and the whole experience was amazing too. Unfortunately, I didn’t get to visit the hippo and elephant areas, and the butterfly and monkey gardens were also closed. Maybe because I came around 5–6 PM, not really sure about the timings though.\nOverall, the environment and surroundings were so peaceful and beautiful, and the ticket price was also very affordable. I would rate it 9.5/10. Will definitely visit again in the daytime soon ?\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-23T00:55:28.406362780Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Brett Kahr\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXC_UVogNlFWFdNaPl1BewhwGKsTDEhWoDMPpP0kpt6h5iAGIzf=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:504:\"The Manila Zoo looks like it was once amazing, which my filipina wife confirmed. However, while still nice, it looks like it suffers from inadequate funding and is missing a lot of the major animals it once had like elephants, giraffes, hippos, and great apes. It does still have its big cats however and a very beautiful art gallery made from butterflies. It still has an aviary, smaller primates and a butterfly garden as well. It was like 20 dollars US for 4 adults so it\'s not expensive for tourists.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-10T11:57:37.667451528Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:87:\"5.5-hectare zoo & garden featuring diverse animals in modest, old-fashioned enclosures.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:15;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY\";s:4:\"name\";s:47:\"William A. Jones Memorial Bridge (Jones Bridge)\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.595792099999999;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.97722220000001;s:7:\"address\";s:53:\"Jones Brg, Binondo, Manila, Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.6;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:2077;s:7:\"reviews\";i:2077;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:477:\"places/ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY/photos/AVoNoXT8eo7baNLb4YS-pZ70sHffZcr0smkLBTWs18iRSYxc0HlU_AzHZ-4FMNIbqouB123LMKl-YYpuJxCEhp_QfZtyKXWrcRVwOL4rRRM9Mvnw3G-qp49s0c9IREwIFGxGnOFB5EjAcN4ivEDcyMbWqLWpM6u5GJ-GgHYFnCwXfhLTlsyJkZ642rwIYyhJHW42isaclGxWkNKbKN3EuYTx7Oztkrf4vELLpJawusShTJhWB8CGR04FJVv4shrBgQauRaBiVCtknoogcxxzbXlejdtkWcw-8huvd0W3TYvfj4GgIEf5P4jtrECuVF0ZAn4NuBOpstkQe7A3EjLIOFAPbnsTlV0pBR0zmZA7L8UI577qwANwgdpFGb_qaBGp0Xde8fmSRXsDl76NDfS2j8eS4durhDeFvL_IC0Qa2CHJKsiFCo0\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:477:\"places/ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY/photos/AVoNoXT8eo7baNLb4YS-pZ70sHffZcr0smkLBTWs18iRSYxc0HlU_AzHZ-4FMNIbqouB123LMKl-YYpuJxCEhp_QfZtyKXWrcRVwOL4rRRM9Mvnw3G-qp49s0c9IREwIFGxGnOFB5EjAcN4ivEDcyMbWqLWpM6u5GJ-GgHYFnCwXfhLTlsyJkZ642rwIYyhJHW42isaclGxWkNKbKN3EuYTx7Oztkrf4vELLpJawusShTJhWB8CGR04FJVv4shrBgQauRaBiVCtknoogcxxzbXlejdtkWcw-8huvd0W3TYvfj4GgIEf5P4jtrECuVF0ZAn4NuBOpstkQe7A3EjLIOFAPbnsTlV0pBR0zmZA7L8UI577qwANwgdpFGb_qaBGp0Xde8fmSRXsDl76NDfS2j8eS4durhDeFvL_IC0Qa2CHJKsiFCo0\";i:1;s:473:\"places/ChIJ3ekUHhrKlzMR9Tn7K6JBUBY/photos/AVoNoXT_BgVbyQhx_JkvvAYvzS6h77b04Xwk7DTLGhW93XlL5PSvfYDJ_iDuDTTkGOkQ9V4HKvcI5UkrKdZ0_KhvSPdHWEf6UcwY3_kmHYDi2ems2Diep3I-FjAJMPmjfjeKz2zxDdRliIZg3uaKL2oYpzsebpwrBcLR3NOazjGbOoRbll4-B7Y2Rci8iDGCOKR-CbnuGS8zdWV0DoGNLqmIr2fEj