entury Roman Catholic church in Intramuros, Manila. It is one of the Philippine churches that falls under the  Baroque Churches of the Philippines, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. It is also the oldest church in the Philippines. There is an old Baroque pipe organ inside of the church upstairs which I found very impressive to see. You can check the nave of the church for free, but if you want to explore the other areas you must pay an entrance fee which is totally worth it as you can go upstairs and see the pipe organ and other artifacts on display at other sections of the church.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-17T08:43:22.874097509Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:19:\"Mabriene Villanueva\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUbVpuDA5reLceSimjcsfrCvBtAOlWjwzwWKg6RM7NvETfvjQ8AQw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:693:\"I had a peaceful and meaningful visit at San Agustin Church. The church is truly a masterpiece, rich in history and beautifully preserved through the years. From its stunning architecture to its calm and solemn atmosphere, you can really feel a deep sense of spirituality the moment you step inside.\n\nI admire how well-maintained the church is despite its age. It stands as a strong symbol of faith and resilience, especially knowing it has withstood many historical events. Whether you come to pray, attend mass, or simply appreciate its beauty, the experience is always memorable and uplifting.\n\nA must-visit place for anyone who wants to connect with history, culture, and faith all in one.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-03T05:32:54.488743837Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:23:\"Mga Rampa ni Tita Marcy\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJPijTT1uPvXSCPVezT4Rn1q5_v74AgBuIX6rSc0Fe_UhkqTg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:337:\"My very first time visiting San Agustin Church, and wow—I am officially in love! ?✨ Walking inside felt like stepping straight into a time machine. I absolutely adored the beautiful, nostalgic vibes and how every single corner is just bursting with history. Such a magical experience! ⛪️ Historic charm at its absolute finest!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-17T10:05:37.828643416Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"keneth perez\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWMm53oVau4YLHDEx3toTLl8C6P4_kYCMVOEC8sAvgQQ2tAVp4A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:228:\"This was our first stop in our mini tour. I went to light some candles, offered my prayers.\nReminder to those who will visit, follow the signages/reminders and be mindful of the volume of your voice inside the church. Thank you.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-31T08:19:42.624009495Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Rizalinda De Ramos\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXTUzW-kdudVsJBtrnXZOHyRujg80fG5ZR4okleGLaQeYRUyL0=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:257:\"Solemn place for worship. Language use during mass is conducive for the local community and for foreign tourists who want to attend mass. Spacious and the architecture of this place was superb. The building mas maintained even it is hundred years ago built.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-31T22:42:02.087249124Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:99:\"Historic church constructed starting in the 16th century with vaulted ceilings & detailed frescoes.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:18;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ3RYFfo-2lzMRWTnOOxDAO18\";s:4:\"name\";s:26:\"Balintawak Cloverleaf Park\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.656937699999999;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.9996183;s:7:\"address\";s:66:\"MX4X+QRH, A. Bonifacio Ave, Quezon City, Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"