:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:19:\"Dennis Rey Loterina\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:119:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWWEh2fr1lqFwRTfqh7Q44TJ0KB4TJHjsT13hjJMULv9oPL9xcB=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:169:\"clean and very accomodating staffs\nthere\'s a 10 minute hike going to the falls\nthe water is crystal clear unless there\'s so much people swimming then it may blurry a bit\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-21T07:58:07.868633598Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:1:\"B\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW3kKDsd1XZvGBBeOURBlHw9t9cz_xbz6wmlEfHmSlJHWwHoooO=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:403:\"The water is refreshing, cool and blue. It’s a small beautiful waterfall with a deep river. But the only problem I had with it, was finding it. I don’t mind a hike but you can easily get lost on the way there and go into someone’s property. Thankfully the locals are super nice in giving directions. I wish they would put some signs up to give you some clear directions on how to get to the falls.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2024-12-18T02:20:13.202306Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:28:\"Arleen Marie Ignacio Salcedo\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:121:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW1l2uZ5awgNMZ1pwS0cyf3tok_9onbHYYd1F7RkTVuA3XCiytbdg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:304:\"Water is cold and not so deep. For a non-swimmer, I was able to enjoy this place. Area is clean and people are warm.\n\nNo signal tho. And food is expensive so bring your own. Kid friendly as waters are shallow in some parts specially near the kubos.\n\nParking is good. Plenty of spaces for motors and cars.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-10-30T00:50:36.269386818Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:14:\"Darryn Sanders\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV3LoFil2GoFF2sd6KEiBLGSlfoYx9emqlhNpOM2kxW2PBXmdcsbA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:374:\"It\'s a decent hike. The drive there has some beautiful views and scenery.\n\nThe falls itself is cool looking, it\'s definitely not a large water fall. The hike isn\'t going to be for everyone, lots of rocks and boulders to navigate.\n\nIt would be wonderful if they would pick up the garbage that is strewn about. That\'s just a typical issue in the Philippines for the most part.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2023-04-07T15:21:58.867409Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:16:\"Mikaela Urmeneta\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWjHGgOiKfq4X-Vb6PMeknfOHmOjcVA8obSr0kqM-6T9bciKMcX=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:386:\"Celebrated my birthday here. We travelled for about half hour from San Clemente town proper. The road is pretty decent. Just be ready because authorities will look for vaccination card and government id upon entering and a payment of ₱20/ person for environmental fee. The 15 minutes walk from cottage is worth it. As you can see, the water is clear and clean. So refreshing. ??\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2022-02-27T07:55:17.590261Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";N;s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:1;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ2_W08chSkTMR38yBJPaMrx4\";s:4:\"name\";s:36:\"Manleluag Spring Protected Landscape\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.7027572;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.2824821;s:7:\"address\";s:45:\"P73J+4X5, Mangatarem, Pangasinan, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.5;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:58;s:7:\"reviews\";i:58;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:478:\"places/ChIJ2_W08chSkTMR38yBJPaMrx4/photos/AVoNoXQGWvDrR0CcyJvYePKfNUvmJlZd9hNhOCrc3pQWQRZApnbiGMtG8r6XukO9VKmk6hmPTfvvqybYtv5uwlMspu-7nRScFoXy-zckHTiqmAMaDPtykzNW9SD1kfPwboLe0HkWB38Vkn-jQIWNQ7-HizfL4Lrm9sGGkaPy9ndz5ebO0wY2J